-- A GUARDIAN OF RECORD. Everything below the first four fields is the
-- Guardianship of Infants Act's own subject matter — security, dealings with
-- the infant's property, maintenance — and no rule in THIS module reads any of
-- it. It is spelled out because L4 has no record-update operator, and it is
-- set to the not-in-evidence value throughout. The four fields this module
-- does read are the parameters: who he is, whose guardian he is, how he came
-- to be one (read by nothing here, and carried so that a reader can see the
-- route was not asserted by accident), and of the person or of the property.
-- `removed from his guardianship by the court` is the fifth, and it is a
-- parameter because s 21(2) turns on it.
GIVEN p IS A Person
      `the reference for the infant of whom he is guardian` IS A STRING
      `how he was appointed` IS A `How the guardian was appointed`
      `of the person or of the property, or both` IS A `Kind of guardianship`
      `has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Guardian
`a PAA guardian` p `the reference for the infant of whom he is guardian` `how he was appointed` `of the person or of the property, or both` `has been removed` MEANS
    Guardian WITH
        `the guardian` IS p
        `the reference for the infant` IS `the reference for the infant of whom he is guardian`
        `how the guardian was appointed` IS `how he was appointed`
        `of the person or of the property` IS `of the person or of the property, or both`
        `alone or jointly` IS `alone`
        `refuses to act` IS FALSE
        `the mother or father objects to his so acting` IS FALSE
        `considers that the mother or father is unfit to have the custody of the infant` IS FALSE
        `removed from his guardianship by the court` IS `has been removed`
        `has given security` IS FALSE
        `the court has otherwise ordered as to security` IS FALSE
        `has sold, mortgaged, exchanged, or otherwise parted with the possession of any of the movable or immovable property of the infant` IS FALSE
        `has leased land belonging to the infant` IS FALSE
        `the term of the lease, in years` IS NOTHING
        `has the permission of the court to deal with the property of the infant` IS FALSE
        `has given a good discharge for a legacy or other capital moneys payable to or receivable by the infant` IS FALSE
        `the court has otherwise ordered as to giving a good discharge` IS FALSE
        `the provision made out of the income of the property of the infant for his maintenance and education` IS
            `A periodical sum` WITH
                `the sum` IS 0
                `the period` IS `monthly`
        `has the permission of the court to apply a sum exceeding $100 per month` IS FALSE

