      `the outcome` IS A `What became of the application`
GIVETH A `Probate application`
`a PAA application by` a `the kind applied for` `the date applied` `the outcome` MEANS
    `Probate application` WITH
        `the applicant` IS a
        `the grant applied for` IS `the kind applied for`
        `the date of the application` IS `the date applied`
        `what became of the application` IS `the outcome`

GIVEN p IS A Person
      f IS A Family
      e IS AN Estate
      w IS A MAYBE Will
      `the grants` IS A LIST OF Grant
      `the applications` IS A LIST OF `Probate application`
      `the infants` IS A LIST OF Infant
      `a claim has been made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Deceased person`
`a PAA deceased person` p f e w `the grants` `the applications` `the infants` `a claim has been made out` MEANS
    `Deceased person` WITH
        `the deceased` IS p
        `the family` IS f
        `the estate` IS e
        `the will` IS w
        `domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death` IS TRUE
        `carried on business or resided in Singapore within 12 months of his death` IS TRUE
        `a Muslim` IS FALSE
        `the grants made in respect of the estate` IS `the grants`
        `the probate applications made in respect of the estate` IS `the applications`
        `a next of kin, creditor or other person has appeared and made out a claim to letters of administration` IS `a claim has been made out`
        `the infants concerned in the estate` IS `the infants`

`the further facts, nothing being made out` MEANS
    `The further facts on which the grant machinery turns` WITH
        `the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts` IS FALSE
        `the Family Court thinks fit to require such security` IS FALSE
        `there is danger that the property may be wasted` IS FALSE
        `it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate` IS FALSE
        `the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property` IS FALSE


§§ `Scenario A — an intestacy, with a surviving spouse and an infant child`

-- Tan Ah Kow died on 15 January 2025 leaving no will, a surviving wife, an
-- adult son and an infant daughter, and $120,000 of movable property in
-- Singapore. This scenario exercises ss 6, 18, 19, 21, 29 and 55.
--
-- EVERY DIRECTIVE BELOW IS AN `#ASSERT` AND NOT AN `#EVAL`, save where the
-- value has no statable expectation — a `DEONTIC`, which cannot be
-- `EQUALS`-compared, and the `#TRACE`s that exercise one. The expected answer
-- was written down from the SECTION first and the file run afterwards, which
-- is the only order in which an assertion can find anything: an assertion
-- copied from what the evaluator already printed blesses the bug along with
-- the rule. Where an assertion turns on a threshold — a count of grantees, a
-- dollar figure, a number of months, a date — BOTH sides of the boundary are
-- asserted, because a suite that only walks the happy path cannot fail.
--
-- AND THE COVERAGE IS MEASURED BY MUTATION, NOT BY THE COUNT. A green count is
-- not evidence: an assertion that would pass whatever the rule did passes
-- exactly as green as one that would not. So every conjunct and disjunct in
-- every decision above was replaced, one at a time, with the identity element
-- of its chain — TRUE in an AND-chain, FALSE in an OR-chain — and the whole
-- suite re-run. A conjunct whose deletion leaves the suite green has no test,
-- and the fixtures below were written until only four such conjuncts remained.
--
-- THE FOUR THAT REMAIN ARE NOT GAPS BUT FACTS ABOUT THE ACT, and each is named
-- at its own site:
--   s 13(1)(a) in the gate's disjunction. Its case — a will appointing no
--     executor — satisfies limbs (b), (d) and (e) vacuously, which is
--     AMBIGUITY A10 and is the reason A10 exists.
--   s 13(1)(c) in the same disjunction. An executor who did not survive the
--     testator necessarily died before obtaining probate, so limb (d) fires,
--     and necessarily did not extract probate, so limb (e) fires.
--   s 55(1)(f)'s "all have died". That conjunct and the six-month conjunct
--     beside it are both `all` over the same list of representatives, and a
--     living representative has no date of death, so no fixture can fail one
--     without failing the other.
--   s 21(2)'s opening "Where an infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled
--     to probate or letters of administration". Once that rule was made to read
--     the GRANTEE, this conjunct became implied by the grantee limb — which
--     asks the same counterfactual of the particular infant the grant names —
--     so no fixture can fail the opening words without also failing the
--     grantee. It is kept because it is the subsection's own opening words and
--     dropping it would leave the encoding reading the Where-clause only
--     through a later limb.
--
-- OVER-DETERMINED NEGATIVES ARE LABELLED AS SUCH. Where a negative assertion is
-- kept because it is the realistic case although more than one limb fails on
-- it, the comment beside it says so and points to the minimal pair that does
-- test the limb. A negative whose comment names one limb and whose fixture
-- fails two is a claim about the rule that the assertion does not support.

`Tan Ah Kow` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei`, `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

`Lim Mei Ling` MEANS `a PAA adult` "Lim Mei Ling" "lim"
`Tan Wei`      MEANS `a PAA adult` "Tan Wei" "wei"
`Tan Xin`      MEANS `a PAA minor` "Tan Xin" "xin"
`Public Trustee as grantee` MEANS `the Public Trustee`
`Acme Trust Company` MEANS
    `a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005` "Acme Trust Company Pte Ltd"

`the estate of Tan Ah Kow` MEANS `a PAA estate` 120_000 0 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE

`Tan Ah Kow’s family` MEANS
    `a PAA family` (LIST `a PAA marriage to` `Lim Mei Ling` TRUE) EMPTY

`the Tan intestacy` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE

-- s 18(1) — no will at all, so the person has died intestate on reading A7.
-- The testate half of the pair is asserted in Scenario B, where the will is.
#ASSERT `s 18(1) — the person has died intestate` `the Tan intestacy`

-- s 18(4)(a) — the class is the widow plus the next of kin, and this assertion
-- names all three members in the order the decision builds them: the spouse
-- limb first, then the next-of-kin limb. A stranger is not in it.
#ASSERT `the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a)` `the Tan intestacy` EQUALS
            LIST `Lim Mei Ling`, `Tan Wei`, `Tan Xin`
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy` "lim"
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy` "wei"
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy` "stranger"

-- AMBIGUITY A12 — INTESTATE SUCCESSION ACT s 3's "child", ASSERTED ON THE
-- CLASS IT GOVERNS. Until this block existed the only child constructor in
-- this file set legitimacy TRUE, so no fixture could produce the case the
-- ruling decides and the ruling was assumed rather than tested. The three
-- corners of the definition first.
#ASSERT     `a “child” within the meaning of section 3 of the Intestate Succession Act 1967` (`a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei`)
#ASSERT     `a “child” within the meaning of section 3 of the Intestate Succession Act 1967` (`a PAA adopted child` `Tan Hui, adopted by order of court`)
#ASSERT NOT `a “child” within the meaning of section 3 of the Intestate Succession Act 1967` (`a PAA child neither legitimate nor adopted` `Tan Bao, whose own son is legitimate`)

-- ... and then on the class. Tan Ah Kow leaves no spouse, one child who is
-- neither legitimate nor adopted, and one adopted child. On A12's reading the
-- adopted child is next of kin and the other is not — which is what the
-- Intestate Succession Act itself answers on the same relation, and the
-- disagreement between the two Acts that an earlier draft of this module
-- produced is gone.
`Tan Feng, the son of Tan Bao` MEANS `a PAA adult` "Tan Feng" "feng"
`Tan Bao, whose own son is legitimate` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Bao" "bao" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Feng, the son of Tan Bao`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Tan Hui, adopted by order of court` MEANS `a PAA adult` "Tan Hui" "hui"
`Tan Ah Kow, one child unadopted and illegitimate and one adopted` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA child neither legitimate nor adopted` `Tan Bao, whose own son is legitimate`
            , `a PAA adopted child` `Tan Hui, adopted by order of court`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, one child unadopted and illegitimate and one adopted` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, one child unadopted and illegitimate and one adopted`
        (`a PAA family` EMPTY EMPTY) `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT `the next of kin of the deceased` `the Tan intestacy, one child unadopted and illegitimate and one adopted` EQUALS
            LIST `Tan Hui, adopted by order of court`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy, one child unadopted and illegitimate and one adopted` "bao"
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy, one child unadopted and illegitimate and one adopted` "hui"
-- ... and the WHOLE BRANCH drops with him: Tan Feng is the intestate's
-- grandson in fact, and legitimate as against his own father, but he comes
-- through a parent who is not a "child" and so stands in nobody's place.
-- That is `the child and his descendants` returning EMPTY rather than
-- stepping over the failing generation.
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy, one child unadopted and illegitimate and one adopted` "feng"

-- THE MINIMAL PAIR THAT MAKES IT ONE FIELD. The identical Tan Bao, with the
-- identical son, on the identical estate — the only difference is which
-- `Child` record the intestate holds him in. Both come through now, the
-- grandson per stirpes.
`Tan Ah Kow, the same child being legitimate` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Bao, whose own son is legitimate`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the same child being legitimate` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the same child being legitimate`
        (`a PAA family` EMPTY EMPTY) `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT `the next of kin of the deceased` `the Tan intestacy, the same child being legitimate` EQUALS
            LIST `Tan Bao, whose own son is legitimate`, `Tan Feng, the son of Tan Bao`

-- AND THE RULING PROPAGATES TO s 6(4), which on an intestacy answers
-- "beneficiary" with s 18(4)(a)'s class as its stated proxy. An infant child
-- who is neither legitimate nor adopted is therefore not a beneficiary for
-- s 6(4) either — the answer the Intestate Succession Act gives on the same
-- facts. s 6(2)'s unqualified "if there is a minority" still finds one, on
-- AMBIGUITY A4's wide reading, so the two subsections part company here for a
-- second reason and the pair is the same one fact.
`Tan Ah Kow, the infant daughter neither legitimate nor adopted` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA child neither legitimate nor adopted` `Tan Xin`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the infant daughter neither legitimate nor adopted` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the infant daughter neither legitimate nor adopted`
        (`a PAA family` EMPTY EMPTY) `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary` `the Tan intestacy, the infant daughter neither legitimate nor adopted` `Tan Xin`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary` `the Tan intestacy, the infant daughter neither legitimate nor adopted` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — there is a minority` `the Tan intestacy, the infant daughter neither legitimate nor adopted` `the date of the hearing`

-- SURVIVORSHIP IN THE SPOUSE LIMB, ASSERTED SEPARATELY FROM SUBSISTENCE.
-- `a marriage leaving a husband or widow` has two conjuncts — the marriage was
-- not dissolved or annulled before the death, and the spouse outlived the
-- deceased — and mutation showed the SECOND had no failing case anywhere in
-- the file: it could be deleted and every assertion stayed green. The two
-- fixtures below fail one conjunct each and no more, so each conjunct now has
-- a test of its own. "husband or widow" is a survivor, which is why the second
-- conjunct is there at all.
`Lim Mei Ling, predeceasing her husband` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Lim Mei Ling" "lim" (`died on` (YMD 2024 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Tan Ah Kow’s family, the wife having predeceased him` MEANS
    `a PAA family` (LIST `a PAA marriage to` `Lim Mei Ling, predeceasing her husband` TRUE) EMPTY
`the Tan intestacy, the wife having predeceased` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family, the wife having predeceased him` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
`Tan Ah Kow’s family, the marriage dissolved` MEANS
    `a PAA family` (LIST `a PAA marriage to` `Lim Mei Ling` FALSE) EMPTY
`the Tan intestacy, the marriage dissolved` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family, the marriage dissolved` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy, the wife having predeceased` "lim"
#ASSERT `the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a)` `the Tan intestacy, the wife having predeceased` EQUALS
            LIST `Tan Wei`, `Tan Xin`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy, the marriage dissolved` "lim"

-- SURVIVORSHIP IN THE NEXT-OF-KIN LIMB. "the husband or widow or next of kin"
-- is a class a grant may be MADE to, so a relative who predeceased the
-- intestate is not in it. Give Tan Ah Kow a son who died in 2024 and the son
-- drops out of the class, out of the s 18(4)(d)(i) denominator, and out of
-- s 19's "no person equally entitled". An earlier draft filtered the spouse
-- limb only, so a dead son was still next of kin.
`Tan Wei, predeceasing his father` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Wei" "wei" (`died on` (YMD 2024 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Tan Xin, so desiring` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Xin" "xin" `living` (JUST (YMD 2032 6 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`Tan Ah Kow, the son having predeceased him` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei, predeceasing his father`
            , `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin, so desiring`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the son having predeceased` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the son having predeceased him` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin, so desiring`) FALSE

#ASSERT `the next of kin of the deceased` `the Tan intestacy, the son having predeceased` EQUALS
            LIST `Tan Xin, so desiring`
#ASSERT `the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a)` `the Tan intestacy, the son having predeceased` EQUALS
            LIST `Lim Mei Ling`, `Tan Xin, so desiring`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin`
                `the Tan intestacy, the son having predeceased` "wei"
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin`
                `the Tan intestacy, the son having predeceased` "xin"

-- s 18(4) — with nobody having applied and nobody having made out a claim, TWO
-- classes are open at once: (a), the class being occupied, and (d), by limb
-- (d)(ii). This is the case the LIST return type exists for. (c) does not
-- appear because this estate has no creditor for a grant to be made to.
#ASSERT `s 18(4) — the classes to which letters of administration may be granted` `the Tan intestacy` EQUALS
            LIST `the husband or widow or next of kin or any of them` , `such person as the court thinks fit`
-- ... and with a creditor in the estate, all three are open.
`the Tan intestacy, with a creditor` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family`
        (`a PAA estate` 120_000 0 0 0 0 (LIST `a PAA creditor` `Chan Kok Wai` 9_000 FALSE) FALSE)
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(4) — the classes to which letters of administration may be granted` `the Tan intestacy, with a creditor` EQUALS
            LIST `the husband or widow or next of kin or any of them` , `a creditor of the deceased, no such person having applied` , `such person as the court thinks fit`

-- ... and where NOBODY survives to fill limb (a) — no spouse, and the only
-- child dead before his father — limb (a) closes and only (d) is left open.
-- Before the survivorship filter this estate reported class (a) OPEN with
-- nobody alive to take it, which is the defect the filter repairs.
`Tan Ah Kow, unmarried, his only child having predeceased him` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei, predeceasing his father`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, nobody surviving to take` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, unmarried, his only child having predeceased him`
        (`a PAA family` EMPTY EMPTY) `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT `the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a)` `the Tan intestacy, nobody surviving to take` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 18(4) — the classes to which letters of administration may be granted` `the Tan intestacy, nobody surviving to take` EQUALS
            LIST `such person as the court thinks fit`

-- ... and once the widow applies, (c) closes, because it is expressly
-- conditioned on "when no such person applies".
`the Tan intestacy, the widow having applied` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA application by` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `letters of administration` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `still pending`)
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(b) — such persons apply for letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having applied`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(b) — such persons apply for letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(c) — no such person applies, and letters of administration may be granted to a creditor of the deceased`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow having applied`
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(c) — no such person applies, and letters of administration may be granted to a creditor of the deceased`
                `the Tan intestacy`
#ASSERT `s 18(4) — the classes to which letters of administration may be granted` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having applied` EQUALS
            LIST `the husband or widow or next of kin or any of them`

-- s 18(4)(d)(ii) — "no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and
-- makes out a claim". Made out where nobody has appeared; not made out where
-- somebody has, which is the second fixture's last field.
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(d)(ii) — no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and makes out a claim to letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(d)(ii) — no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and makes out a claim to letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having applied`

-- s 18(4)(d)(i) — "the greater number of such next of kin, so desire", read as
-- a MAJORITY OF ALL under AMBIGUITY A8. Both sides of that majority are
-- asserted: of two next of kin, none desiring and one desiring both fail, two
-- desiring succeeds, and one of ONE succeeds. The limb is also FALSE where
-- there are no next of kin at all, "such next of kin" presupposing some.
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire` `the Tan intestacy`

`Tan Wei, so desiring` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Wei" "wei" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`Tan Ah Kow, the children so desiring` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei, so desiring`, `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin, so desiring`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the children so desiring` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the children so desiring` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin, so desiring`) FALSE
`Tan Ah Kow, one child so desiring` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei`, `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin, so desiring`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, one child so desiring` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, one child so desiring` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin, so desiring`) FALSE

#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire` `the Tan intestacy, the children so desiring`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire` `the Tan intestacy, one child so desiring`
-- ONE OF ONE IS A MAJORITY, and this is the assertion the survivorship filter
-- had to be repaired to satisfy: the dead son used to sit in the denominator,
-- so his silence defeated the unanimous wish of every living next of kin.
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire` `the Tan intestacy, the son having predeceased`
-- ... and with no next of kin at all, the limb cannot be made out.
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire` `the Tan intestacy, nobody surviving to take`

-- s 18(4)(d) — THE DISJUNCTION, WITH EACH LIMB CARRYING IT ALONE. Every fixture
-- above has `a claim has been made out` FALSE, so limb (ii) was satisfied
-- wherever (i) was and (i) could be deleted from the disjunction with the suite
-- staying green. The fixture below makes limb (ii) FALSE — somebody HAS
-- appeared and made out a claim — and leaves (i) to carry the subsection on its
-- own.
`the Tan intestacy, the children so desiring, a claim having been made out` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the children so desiring` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin, so desiring`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(d)(ii) — no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and makes out a claim to letters of administration`
                `the Tan intestacy, the children so desiring, a claim having been made out`
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire`
                `the Tan intestacy, the children so desiring, a claim having been made out`
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(d) — letters of administration may be granted to such person as the court thinks fit`
                `the Tan intestacy, the children so desiring, a claim having been made out`
-- ... and with neither limb, the subsection is not made out: nobody so desires,
-- and a claim has been made out.
`the Tan intestacy, nobody desiring, a claim having been made out` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(d) — letters of administration may be granted to such person as the court thinks fit`
                `the Tan intestacy, nobody desiring, a claim having been made out`
-- ... and limb (ii) alone carries it where nobody desires and nobody has
-- appeared, which is the plain s 18(4)(d)(ii) case.
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(d) — letters of administration may be granted to such person as the court thinks fit` `the Tan intestacy`

§§ `Scenario A — sections 6 and 21 over the same estate`

-- s 6(2) — there IS a minority, Tan Xin attaining majority in 2032.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) — there is a minority` `the Tan intestacy` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and no life interest, there being no will. The life-interest limb is
-- exercised on its own facts in Scenario B.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — a life interest arises under the will` `the Tan intestacy`
#ASSERT `s 6(2) — the requirement as to the grantees is engaged` `the Tan intestacy` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and on an estate with neither, the requirement is not engaged at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — the requirement as to the grantees is engaged` (`the Ong estate with` NOTHING EMPTY) `the date of the hearing`

`a grant to the widow alone` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE

`a grant to the widow and the son` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Tan Wei`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE

