-- s 6(1) — "not ... to more than 4 persons". BOTH SIDES OF THE CEILING: two is
-- fine, four is fine, five is not. Four is the assertion that would catch an
-- off-by-one written as `AT LEAST 4`.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons in respect of the same property` `a grant to the widow and the son`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons in respect of the same property` `a grant to four persons`
#ASSERT     `s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons in respect of the same property` `a grant to five persons`

-- s 6(2) — "not less than 2 individuals", and both sides of THAT threshold:
-- the widow alone does not satisfy it while the minority subsists; the widow
-- with the son does; and the widow with a trust company does too, on the first
-- limb, "a trust corporation, with or without an individual".
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — the grant complies with section 6(2)` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow alone` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — the grant complies with section 6(2)` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow and the son` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — the grant complies with section 6(2)` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow and a trust company` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — granted either to a trust corporation, with or without an individual, or to not less than 2 individuals` `a grant to the widow alone`
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — granted either to a trust corporation, with or without an individual, or to not less than 2 individuals` `a grant to the widow and the son`

-- ... and once the child has attained majority the requirement is not engaged
-- at all, so a sole administrator complies. Read at 1 January 2033.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — there is a minority` `the Tan intestacy` (YMD 2033 1 1)
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — the grant complies with section 6(2)` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow alone` (YMD 2033 1 1)

-- ... and a grant of PROBATE is not one of the grants s 6(2) governs on either
-- reading of AMBIGUITY A5, so it complies vacuously.
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — the grant is one of the grants section 6(2) governs` `a grant to the widow alone`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — the grant is one of the grants section 6(2) governs` `a grant of probate to Chan alone`

-- s 6(6) — the three cases the definition distinguishes.
#ASSERT     `s 6(6) — a trust corporation` `Public Trustee as grantee`
#ASSERT     `s 6(6) — a trust corporation` `Acme Trust Company`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(6) — a trust corporation` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`)
-- ... and the Government, which is in `Person or corporation` for the Intestate
-- Succession Act's rule 9 and which s 6(6) does not name.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(6) — a trust corporation` `the Government`

-- s 6(4) — the widow is the sole personal representative, a minority of a
-- BENEFICIARY subsists (Tan Xin being next of kin on this intestacy) and the
-- estate is not fully administered, so the window is open.
`the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING (LIST `a grant to the widow alone`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` `Tan Xin`
#ASSERT `s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and it closes once the child is of age.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` (YMD 2033 1 1)
-- ... and it closes on the count of representatives too: with TWO, s 6(4) has
-- nothing to add a representative to.
`the Tan intestacy, two administrators having taken a grant` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING (LIST `a grant to the widow and the son`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Tan intestacy, two administrators having taken a grant` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and where the estate is fully administered, the closing words shut it.
`the Tan intestacy, fully administered` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` (`a PAA estate` 120_000 0 0 0 0 EMPTY TRUE)
        NOTHING (LIST `a grant to the widow alone`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Tan intestacy, fully administered` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... and the PARENTHESIS, "(not being a trust corporation)", which had no
-- failing case anywhere in the file: no fixture gave an estate a SOLE
-- trust-corporation personal representative, so the conjunct could be deleted
-- with every assertion staying green. This estate differs from
-- `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` — which opens the window
-- — in exactly one fact: who the sole administrator is. The minority, the
-- count of one, and the unadministered estate are all unchanged, so the
-- parenthesis is the only thing that can shut it.
`a grant to a trust company alone` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` `Acme Trust Company` `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, a trust company having taken a grant` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING (LIST `a grant to a trust company alone`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary` `the Tan intestacy, a trust company having taken a grant` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT count (`the personal representatives of the estate still living` `the Tan intestacy, a trust company having taken a grant`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Tan intestacy, a trust company having taken a grant` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... and "only one personal representative" IS COUNTED OVER THE LIVING ONES.
-- A grant to two administrators, one of whom has since died, leaves the estate
-- with one representative — that is what s 25(1) says accrual does — and the
-- s 6(4) window is therefore OPEN on it. An earlier draft counted the dead
-- grantee, reported two, and shut the window in exactly the case the
-- subsection exists for: an infant beneficiary and a single administrator.
-- The contrast with `the Tan intestacy, two administrators having taken a
-- grant` above is one fact, the second administrator's death.
`the Tan intestacy, one of two administrators having died` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING (LIST `letters to two administrators, one having died`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT count (`the personal representatives of the estate` `the Tan intestacy, one of two administrators having died`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT count (`the personal representatives of the estate still living` `the Tan intestacy, one of two administrators having died`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Tan intestacy, one of two administrators having died` `the date of the hearing`

