#ASSERT NOT `s 6(5) — this section applies to the grant` `a grant of no recorded date`

-- s 21(1) — the bar bites on the infant daughter and not on the adult son.
-- AMBIGUITY A2: a person whose date of majority is not in evidence is NOT
-- shown to be an infant, so the bar does not bite on him either.
#ASSERT     `s 21(1) — no probate or letters of administration shall be granted to a person while he is an infant` `Tan Xin` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(1) — no probate or letters of administration shall be granted to a person while he is an infant` `Tan Wei` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(1) — no probate or letters of administration shall be granted to a person while he is an infant` (`a PAA person of unknown age` "Unknown" "unk") `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and both sides of the day the infancy ends. Tan Xin attains her majority
-- on 1 June 2032: the bar bites on 31 May and not on the day itself.
#ASSERT     `s 21(1) — no probate or letters of administration shall be granted to a person while he is an infant` `Tan Xin` (YMD 2032 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(1) — no probate or letters of administration shall be granted to a person while he is an infant` `Tan Xin` (YMD 2032 6 1)

-- s 21(2) — Tan Xin would, but for her infancy, be entitled: she is next of kin
-- on an intestacy, so letters of administration would be open to her. An infant
-- who is neither an executor appointed by a will nor within the s 18(4)(a)
-- class would not be, however infant he is.
#ASSERT `s 21(2) — this infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy` (`a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — this infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy` (`a PAA infant concerned in the estate` (`a PAA minor` "Unrelated Infant" "uri")) `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and an ADULT in the same class is not within s 21(2) at all, the
-- subsection opening "Where an infant would".
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — this infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy` (`a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Wei`) `the date of the hearing`

-- s 21(2), THE GRANT RULE — FIVE THINGS THE SUBSECTION FIXES: an infant so
-- entitled, the kind of grant, the subjection to s 6(1), the grantee, and the
-- limitation. Each is asserted by its own failing case, and the failing case
-- differs from the passing one in ONE fact wherever a fixture can be built
-- that way.
--
-- THE ESTATE THE POSITIVE CASE NEEDS. Every other fixture in this file leaves
-- `the guardians of the infant` empty, which is why the grantee limb had no
-- case at all until now. Lim Mei Ling is Tan Xin's mother and Tan Ah Kow is
-- dead, which is the Guardianship of Infants Act s 6(1) situation; the fixture
-- records her as guardian of the person AND property, that being the kind
-- s 21(2) names. The appointment route is recorded and read by nothing here —
-- see the note at `is this guardian of the person and property of the infant`.
`the widow, guardian of the person and property of Tan Xin` MEANS
    `a PAA guardian` `Lim Mei Ling` "xin" `guardian by virtue of surviving the other parent`
        `guardian of the person and property of the infant` FALSE
`the widow, guardian of the property of Tan Xin only` MEANS
    `a PAA guardian` `Lim Mei Ling` "xin" `guardian by virtue of surviving the other parent`
        `guardian of the property of the infant` FALSE
`the widow, since removed from her guardianship of Tan Xin` MEANS
    `a PAA guardian` `Lim Mei Ling` "xin" `guardian by virtue of surviving the other parent`
        `guardian of the person and property of the infant` TRUE

`the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the infant` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate, with guardians` `Tan Xin`
                  (LIST `the widow, guardian of the person and property of Tan Xin`)) FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the property only` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate, with guardians` `Tan Xin`
                  (LIST `the widow, guardian of the property of Tan Xin only`)) FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the widow having been removed from her guardianship` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate, with guardians` `Tan Xin`
                  (LIST `the widow, since removed from her guardianship of Tan Xin`)) FALSE

