-- THE POSITIVE CASE. All five limbs made out.
#ASSERT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
            `the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the infant`
            `a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until the infant obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... the LIMITATION, on its own: the same estate, the same grantee in the
-- same capacity, and the grant `not limited`. s 21(2) says the grant is
-- "limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself" and a grant that is
-- not so limited is not a grant this subsection authorises. An earlier draft
-- omitted this conjunct and answered TRUE here.
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the infant`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, not limited` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... the CAPACITY, on its own: the same estate, the same widow, the same
-- limitation, the same pointer to the same infant — and the grant made to her
-- as administrator rather than as guardian. The subsection's first limb names
-- the guardian, and this decision answers that limb only.
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the infant`
                `a grant to the widow as administrator, limited until the infant obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... the POINTER, on its own: the same grant in the guardian's capacity, for
-- the use and benefit of the ADULT son. He is not an infant so entitled, so
-- the widow's guardianship of Tan Xin does not open a grant for him.
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the infant`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, for the use and benefit of the adult son` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... the GUARDIANSHIP ITSELF, on its own, three ways over the same grant.
-- With no guardian of record the widow is a stranger to the office; a guardian
-- of the PROPERTY only is not the person s 21(2) names, the subsection saying
-- "of the person and property"; and a guardian the court has removed under
-- Guardianship of Infants Act s 10 is not the guardian at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until the infant obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the property only`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until the infant obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow having been removed from her guardianship`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until the infant obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... a GUARDIAN WHO IS NOT THIS GRANTEE. Tan Xin has a guardian of the person
