#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant of probate to Chan alone` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... and "with or without the will annexed" reaches BOTH kinds, which no
-- fixture exercised: every s 21(2) case above is a grant of letters of
-- administration simpliciter, so the second disjunct could be deleted unnoticed.
-- The infant here is an executor appointed by the will, so the grant that
-- follows is one WITH the will annexed. Goh Siew Lan is his guardian; the
-- route recorded is a will, which is Guardianship of Infants Act s 7(1) and
-- Wills Act s 27(3) territory and is read by nothing in this module.
`Goh, guardian of the person and property of the infant executor` MEANS
    `a PAA guardian` `Goh Siew Lan` "ngwj" `appointed by the father by will`
        `guardian of the person and property of the infant` FALSE
`letters with the will annexed to Goh as guardian of the infant executor` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Goh Siew Lan`) `as the guardian of the person and property of the infant` (JUST "ngwj"))
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1))
        (`limited in some other way` "limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself")
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`the Ong testacy, an infant executor with a guardian, Goh administering` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon`
        (JUST `the will appointing an infant executor`)
        (LIST `letters with the will annexed to Goh as guardian of the infant executor`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate, with guardians` `Ng Wei Jie, an infant executor`
                  (LIST `Goh, guardian of the person and property of the infant executor`)) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
            `the Ong testacy, an infant executor with a guardian, Goh administering`
            `letters with the will annexed to Goh as guardian of the infant executor` `the date of the hearing`

-- s 21(3) — with ONE infant so entitled the limitation runs until she takes a
-- grant; with TWO it runs until ANY of them does. This is the whole of s 21(3),
-- and the count is asserted on both sides of its "2 or more".
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(3) — there are 2 or more infant executors or persons so entitled` `the Tan intestacy` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the limitation on a grant made under subsection (2)` `the Tan intestacy` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `limited in some other way` "limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself"

`Tan Xin’s infant brother` MEANS `a PAA minor` "Tan Yong" "yong"
`Tan Ah Kow, with two infant children` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin`, `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin’s infant brother`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, two infants entitled` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, with two infant children` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`
            , `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin’s infant brother`) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(3) — there are 2 or more infant executors or persons so entitled` `the Tan intestacy, two infants entitled` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the limitation on a grant made under subsection (2)` `the Tan intestacy, two infants entitled` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `limited in some other way` "limited until any of them obtains a grant"

-- ... AND s 21(3) IS LIVE IN THE GRANT RULE, which is the whole reason s 21(2)
-- reads the limitation at all. The same estate, the same widow as guardian of
-- Tan Xin, the same capacity and pointer — and the two grants differ only in
-- the words of the limitation. With two infants so entitled, the grant that
-- runs "until the infant obtains a grant to himself" is NOT a grant made under
-- subsection (2) and the one that runs "until any of them obtains a grant" is.
-- On the one-infant estate above the pair is the other way round. That is
-- s 21(3)'s only operation, and it would be inert if the limitation went
-- unread.
`the Tan intestacy, two infants entitled, the widow being guardian of one` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, with two infant children` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate, with guardians` `Tan Xin`
                  (LIST `the widow, guardian of the person and property of Tan Xin`)
            , `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin’s infant brother`) FALSE
`a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until any of them obtains a grant` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as the guardian of the person and property of the infant` (JUST "xin"))
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1))
        (`limited in some other way` "limited until any of them obtains a grant")
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, two infants entitled, the widow being guardian of one`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until the infant obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, two infants entitled, the widow being guardian of one`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until any of them obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and the same two grants on the ONE-infant estate, the other way round.
#ASSERT NOT `s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow being guardian of the infant`
                `a grant to the widow as guardian, limited until any of them obtains a grant` `the date of the hearing`

§§ `Scenario A — section 19, the attorney of an absent person entitled`

-- s 19 has three limbs and each is asserted with a case that fails it: the
-- person must be entitled on an intestacy, must be absent from Singapore, and
-- no person equally entitled must be willing to act.
`Lim Mei Ling, abroad` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Lim Mei Ling" "lim" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`Tan Wei, unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Wei" "wei" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Tan Xin, unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Xin" "xin" `living` (JUST (YMD 2032 6 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a stranger abroad` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Stranger" "str" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`Tan Ah Kow, the children unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei, unwilling`, `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin, unwilling`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Tan Ah Kow’s family, the widow abroad` MEANS
    `a PAA family` (LIST `a PAA marriage to` `Lim Mei Ling, abroad` TRUE) EMPTY
`the Tan intestacy, the widow abroad and the children unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the children unwilling` `Tan Ah Kow’s family, the widow abroad` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin, unwilling`) FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the widow abroad` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family, the widow abroad` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE

#ASSERT `s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person`
            `the Tan intestacy, the widow abroad and the children unwilling` `Lim Mei Ling, abroad`
-- ... but a willing son is a person equally entitled, so the route closes.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow abroad` `Lim Mei Ling, abroad`
-- ... a person not entitled on an intestacy at all is outside the section.
-- OVER-DETERMINED, AND KEPT AS SUCH: on this estate the widow is willing to
-- act, so the stranger fails the THIRD limb as well as the first. It is worth
-- keeping because it is the realistic case, but it does not test the first
-- limb — the minimal pair below does.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow abroad and the children unwilling` `a stranger abroad`
-- ... and so is a person entitled who is not absent.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow abroad and the children unwilling` `Lim Mei Ling`
-- THE MINIMAL PAIR FOR THE FIRST LIMB. On an estate where nobody entitled is
-- willing to act, the third limb is satisfied for everybody, so membership of
-- the s 18(4)(a) class is the only thing left that can decide the section. The
-- widow, who is in it, satisfies s 19; the stranger, who differs from her in
-- that one fact and in no other — both are abroad, both unwilling — does not.
-- Without this pair the first limb could be deleted and the suite stayed green.
`Lim Mei Ling, abroad and unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Lim Mei Ling" "lim" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a stranger abroad and unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Stranger" "str" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`Tan Ah Kow’s family, the widow abroad and unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA family` (LIST `a PAA marriage to` `Lim Mei Ling, abroad and unwilling` TRUE) EMPTY
`the Tan intestacy, nobody entitled being willing to act` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the children unwilling` `Tan Ah Kow’s family, the widow abroad and unwilling`
        `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin, unwilling`) FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person`
                `the Tan intestacy, nobody entitled being willing to act` `Lim Mei Ling, abroad and unwilling`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person`
                `the Tan intestacy, nobody entitled being willing to act` `a stranger abroad and unwilling`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy, nobody entitled being willing to act` "str"

#ASSERT `s 19 — the limitation on a grant to the attorney of an absent person entitled` EQUALS
            `limited in some other way` "limited until he obtains a grant to himself"

§§ `Scenario A — section 18(5), and section 20`

-- s 18(5) is a SAVING for a law outside this Act, and what is encoded is the
-- narrow case the ontology puts in evidence: the deceased being a Muslim. The
-- fixture is spelled as a full record because the constructors above fix
-- `a Muslim` at FALSE.
`the Tan intestacy, the deceased being a Muslim` MEANS
    `Deceased person` WITH
        `the deceased` IS `Tan Ah Kow`
        `the family` IS `Tan Ah Kow’s family`
        `the estate` IS `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        `the will` IS NOTHING
        `domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death` IS TRUE
        `carried on business or resided in Singapore within 12 months of his death` IS TRUE
        `a Muslim` IS TRUE
        `the grants made in respect of the estate` IS EMPTY
        `the probate applications made in respect of the estate` IS EMPTY
        `a next of kin, creditor or other person has appeared and made out a claim to letters of administration` IS FALSE
        `the infants concerned in the estate` IS LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`
#ASSERT     `s 18(5) — a law making special provision regarding the estates of persons of a particular religion or race is in evidence` `the Tan intestacy, the deceased being a Muslim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(5) — a law making special provision regarding the estates of persons of a particular religion or race is in evidence` `the Tan intestacy`

-- s 20 — the gate is the bare fact that a probate action is pending, and the
-- limitation is the Wills Act s 28(4)(b) category.
#ASSERT     `s 20 — letters of administration may be granted pending a probate action` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — letters of administration may be granted pending a probate action` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20 — the limitation on a grant pending a probate action` EQUALS
            `a grant that does not permit the distribution of the testator’s estate`

-- s 17 — two facts, and both are needed: a will that is not forthcoming AND
-- reason to believe one exists.
#ASSERT     `s 17 — letters of administration may be granted, limited until the will is produced` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 17 — letters of administration may be granted, limited until the will is produced` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 17 — letters of administration may be granted, limited until the will is produced` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 — the limitation on a grant until the will is produced` EQUALS
            `limited in some other way` "limited until the will or an authenticated copy thereof is produced"

§§ `Scenario B — a testacy, and the five limbs of section 13(1)`

-- Ong Bee Hoon died on 15 January 2025 leaving a will. Six variants of that
-- will exercise s 13(1) limb by limb, and one variant satisfies no limb at all.

`Ong Bee Hoon` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Ong Bee Hoon" "ong" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1970 1 1))
        EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

`Chan Kok Wai`  MEANS `a PAA adult` "Chan Kok Wai" "chan"
`Goh Siew Lan`  MEANS `a PAA adult` "Goh Siew Lan" "goh"
`Chan, abroad`  MEANS `a PAA person in full` "Chan Kok Wai" "chan" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`Goh, abroad`   MEANS `a PAA person in full` "Goh Siew Lan" "goh" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`Goh, unwilling` MEANS `a PAA person in full` "Goh Siew Lan" "goh" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Chan, lacking capacity` MEANS `a PAA person in full` "Chan Kok Wai" "chan" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a stranger lacking capacity` MEANS `a PAA person in full` "Stranger" "str" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Chan, predeceasing the testator` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Chan Kok Wai" "chan" (`died on` (YMD 2024 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Chan, dying after the testator` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Chan Kok Wai" "chan" (`died on` (YMD 2025 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Goh, dying after the testator` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Goh Siew Lan" "goh" (`died on` (YMD 2025 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

`the estate of Ong Bee Hoon` MEANS `a PAA estate` 400_000 0 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE
`Ong Bee Hoon’s family` MEANS `a PAA family` EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN w IS A MAYBE Will, `the grants` IS A LIST OF Grant
GIVETH A `Deceased person`
`the Ong estate with` w `the grants` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon`
        w `the grants` EMPTY EMPTY FALSE

-- (a) no executor is appointed by a will.
`the will appointing no executor` MEANS `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
-- (b) one executor legally incapable otherwise than under ss 21(1)/22(1),
--     the other having renounced — AMBIGUITY A6's mixed case.
`the will whose executors are disqualified` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
-- (b) again, this time through s 22(1): the executor lacks mental capacity,
--     which `family-domain.l4` deliberately does NOT fold into the residue.
`the will whose sole executor lacks mental capacity` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon` (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, lacking capacity` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
-- (b) and the mixed case's failing partner: one disqualified, one not.
`the will one of whose executors is disqualified` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
-- (c) no executor survives the testator.
`the will whose executor predeceased the testator` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon` (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, predeceasing the testator` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
-- (d) the executor outlived the testator but died without obtaining probate.
`the will whose executor died after the testator` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon` (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EMPTY EMPTY
-- (d) the other disjunct: he obtained probate but had not administered the
--     whole estate when he died.
`the will whose executor died having proved but not administered` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon` (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
-- (e) the executors do not appear and extract probate.
`the will whose executors have not extracted probate` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
-- none: capable, living, unrenounced executors who have extracted probate.
`the will whose executors have all extracted probate` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EMPTY EMPTY

-- s 18(1) — the negative half of the pair asserted in Scenario A: an estate
-- with a will has not "died intestate" on reading A7, and takes the s 13 grant.
#ASSERT NOT `s 18(1) — the person has died intestate` (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have all extracted probate`) EMPTY)

-- Limb by limb, each with the case that satisfies it AND the case that does
-- not. Note that (c) and (d) BOTH fire on the predeceasing executor: he did not
-- survive the testator AND he died without obtaining probate. The limbs overlap
-- in the Act too — they are alternatives, not a partition.
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(a) — no executor is appointed by a will` `the will appointing no executor`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(a) — no executor is appointed by a will` `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such` `the will whose executors are disqualified` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such` `the will whose sole executor lacks mental capacity` `the date of the hearing`
-- AMBIGUITY A6 is per-EXECUTOR and not per-CLASS: the mixed will above satisfies
-- the limb, and this one — where only one of the two is disqualified — does not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such` `the will one of whose executors is disqualified` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such` `the will whose executors have all extracted probate` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator` `the will whose executor predeceased the testator`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator` `the will whose executor died after the testator`
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(e) — the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate` `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(e) — the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate` `the will whose executors have all extracted probate`

-- (d) — the executor died after the testator having "administered all the
-- estate" but never obtaining probate, so the FIRST disjunct of the limb
-- fires. Give him a grant of probate dated in his lifetime and it stops firing.
`a grant of probate to Chan, in his lifetime` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased`
            (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) EMPTY)
            `the will whose executor died after the testator`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Chan, in his lifetime`))
                `the will whose executor died after the testator`
-- ... and the SECOND disjunct on its own: probate obtained in his lifetime, but
-- the estate not fully administered when he died.
#ASSERT `s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased`
            (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died having proved but not administered`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Chan, in his lifetime`))
            `the will whose executor died having proved but not administered`
-- ... and a living executor is outside the limb however little he has done.
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`) EMPTY)
                `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`

-- The gate itself: made out on the (b) will, not made out where every executor
-- is capable, living, unrenounced and has extracted probate.
#ASSERT `s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors`
            (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors are disqualified`) EMPTY)
            `the will whose executors are disqualified` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have all extracted probate`) EMPTY)
                `the will whose executors have all extracted probate` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and AMBIGUITY A10's case: a will appointing no executor satisfies the
-- gate, limb (a) being made out in exactly that case.
#ASSERT `s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors`
            (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will appointing no executor`) EMPTY)
            `the will appointing no executor` `the date of the hearing`

-- THE MACHINERY BEHIND LIMB (d), WHICH HAD NO TEST OF ITS OWN. `a grant of
-- probate obtained by this executor in his lifetime` has four conjuncts and
-- mutation showed that three of them — the revocation filter, the identity of
-- the grantee, and the lifetime comparison — could each be deleted with every
-- assertion in the file staying green, as could the `as executor` conjunct of
-- `this grantee is this executor, taking as executor`. The four grants below
-- each fail exactly one of them against `a grant of probate to Chan, in his
-- lifetime`, which satisfies all four, so limb (d) fires in each case where it
-- did not before.
`a grant of probate to Chan, since revoked` MEANS
    Grant WITH
        `the kind of grant` IS `probate`
        `the grantees` IS LIST (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        `the date of the grant` IS JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)
        `the limitation` IS `not limited`
        `the court that made the grant` IS (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`)
        `the exception subject to which the grant is made` IS NOTHING
        `expired by effluxion of time or by the happening of the event or contingency on which it was limited` IS FALSE
        `revoked` IS TRUE
        `has given such security as is lawfully required to be furnished` IS TRUE
        `has been extracted` IS TRUE
        `sealed under section 47(1) of the Probate and Administration Act 1934` IS FALSE
        `the date of the sealing` IS NOTHING
`a grant of probate to Goh, in Chan’s lifetime` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Goh Siew Lan`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a grant to Chan as administrator, in his lifetime` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a grant of probate to Chan, made after his death` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 8 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Chan, in his lifetime`))
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Chan, since revoked`))
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Goh, in Chan’s lifetime`))
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant to Chan as administrator, in his lifetime`))
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Chan, made after his death`))
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- ... and each of the four therefore turns limb (d) back on, the executor
-- having died without a probate that counts.
#ASSERT `s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased`
            (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Chan, since revoked`))
            `the will whose executor died after the testator`
#ASSERT `s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased`
            (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) (LIST `a grant of probate to Chan, made after his death`))
            `the will whose executor died after the testator`
-- ... and `this grantee is this executor, taking as executor` asserted on its
-- own facts, both conjuncts having a failing case.
#ASSERT     `this grantee is this executor, taking as executor`
                (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as executor` NOTHING)
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `this grantee is this executor, taking as executor`
                (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `this grantee is this executor, taking as executor`
                (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Goh Siew Lan`) `as executor` NOTHING)
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, dying after the testator` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- LIMB (b)'s INFANCY DISJUNCT, which likewise had no test. s 21(1) is one of
-- the three sources of legal incapacity limb (b) reads, and the only fixture
-- with an infant executor never asked limb (b) about him. Ng Wei Jie attains
-- his majority on 1 June 2032, so the same executor answers the same question
-- two ways across that date and nothing else about him changes.
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(b) — this executor is legally incapable of acting as such`
                (`a PAA executor` `Ng Wei Jie, an infant executor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(b) — this executor is legally incapable of acting as such`
                (`a PAA executor` `Ng Wei Jie, an infant executor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2033 1 1)
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such`
                `the will appointing an infant executor` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such`
                `the will appointing an infant executor` (YMD 2033 1 1)

-- THE GATE'S LIMBS, EACH CARRYING IT ALONE where the Act's own overlaps allow.
-- The gate is a disjunction, and a fixture that fires several limbs tests none
-- of them: mutation showed limbs (a) to (d) could each be deleted from it with
-- every assertion staying green.
--
--   (b) ALONE — executors disqualified who HAVE extracted probate, so limb (e)
--       is off, and living, so (c) and (d) are off.
--   (d) ALONE — an executor who outlived the testator (so (c) is off), died
--       without probate, and had extracted probate in the record (so (e) is
--       off).
--   (e) ALONE — living, capable, unrenounced executors who have not extracted.
--
-- (a) AND (c) CANNOT BE ISOLATED, and that is a fact about the Act and not a
-- gap in the fixtures. (a)'s case — a will appointing no executor — satisfies
-- (b), (d) and (e) vacuously, which is AMBIGUITY A10 and is why A10 exists.
-- (c)'s case — an executor who did not survive the testator — necessarily
-- died before obtaining probate, so (d) fires, and necessarily did not extract
-- probate, so (e) fires: the module's own note above says the limbs overlap in
-- the Act too.
`the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT     `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such`
                `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(a) — no executor is appointed by a will` `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator` `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved`) EMPTY)
                `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(e) — the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate`
                `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved`
#ASSERT     `s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved`) EMPTY)
                `the will whose executors are disqualified, both having proved` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... (d) alone.
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(a) — no executor is appointed by a will` `the will whose executor died after the testator`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such`
                `the will whose executor died after the testator` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(e) — the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate`
                `the will whose executor died after the testator`
#ASSERT     `s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) EMPTY)
                `the will whose executor died after the testator` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... (e) alone.
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such`
                `the will whose executors have not extracted probate` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator` `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`
#ASSERT     `s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`) EMPTY)
                `the will whose executors have not extracted probate` `the date of the hearing`

§§ `Scenario B — sections 8, 13(2), 14, 15, 12 and 16`

-- s 8(1) — Chan is an executor appointed by the will; a stranger is not.
#ASSERT     `s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`) EMPTY) "chan"
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`) EMPTY) "stranger"
-- ... and on an intestacy there is no will to be appointed by.
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will` `the Tan intestacy` "wei"

-- s 8(3) — "probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed",
-- but "Subject to section 6". Both halves are asserted: a grant to ONE of the
-- two appointed executors is good, a grant to a stranger is not, and a grant to
-- FIVE appointed executors fails on s 6(1) where a grant to four does not.
`a grant of probate to Chan alone` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a grant of probate to a stranger` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` (`a PAA adult` "Stranger" "str")) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`the will appointing five executors` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` (`a PAA adult` "A" "a") FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` (`a PAA adult` "B" "b") FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` (`a PAA adult` "C" "c") FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
`probate to four of the five executors` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Goh Siew Lan`) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` (`a PAA adult` "A" "a")) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` (`a PAA adult` "B" "b")) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`probate to all five executors` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Goh Siew Lan`) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` (`a PAA adult` "A" "a")) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` (`a PAA adult` "B" "b")) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` (`a PAA adult` "C" "c")) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT     `s 8(3) — probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed, subject to section 6`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`) EMPTY) `a grant of probate to Chan alone`
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(3) — probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed, subject to section 6`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`) EMPTY) `a grant of probate to a stranger`
#ASSERT     `s 8(3) — probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed, subject to section 6`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will appointing five executors`) EMPTY) `probate to four of the five executors`
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(3) — probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed, subject to section 6`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will appointing five executors`) EMPTY) `probate to all five executors`

-- s 13(2) — the ranked class. Chan takes the residue, Goh a beneficial
-- pecuniary legacy, Lim is a creditor, and a stranger stands in no rung.
-- Note that Chan answers BOTH (a) and (d) and the order puts him in (a).
`the will with a residue and a legacy` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE
            , `a PAA gift to` `Goh Siew Lan` `a pecuniary legacy` 20_000 TRUE)
        EMPTY
`the estate of Ong Bee Hoon, with a creditor` MEANS
    `a PAA estate` 400_000 0 0 0 0 (LIST `a PAA creditor` `Lim Mei Ling` 5_000 FALSE) FALSE
`the Ong testacy with a creditor` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon, with a creditor`
        (JUST `the will with a residue and a legacy`) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE

#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` "chan" FALSE EQUALS
            JUST `a universal or residuary legatee`
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` "goh" FALSE EQUALS
            JUST `a legatee having a beneficial interest`
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` "lim" FALSE EQUALS
            JUST `a creditor of the deceased`
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` "stranger" FALSE EQUALS
            NOTHING
-- ... and limb (b), the one fact the shared ontology cannot supply, asserted:
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` "stranger" TRUE EQUALS
            JUST `a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee`

-- RUNG (c) — "such person or persons, being beneficiaries under the will, as
-- would have been entitled to a grant of letters of administration if the
-- deceased had died intestate". It needs a person who is BOTH: a legatee whose
-- gift is not universal or residuary, and within s 18(4)(a)'s class read
-- counterfactually. Ong Bee Hoon's daughter is both, and the order puts her in
-- (c) rather than in (d), where her beneficial legacy would otherwise place her.
`Ong Li Ping` MEANS `a PAA adult` "Ong Li Ping" "ping"
`Ong Bee Hoon, with a daughter` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Ong Bee Hoon" "ong" (`died on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) (JUST (YMD 1970 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Ong Li Ping`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the will giving the daughter a legacy` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon, with a daughter`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE
            , `a PAA gift to` `Ong Li Ping` `a pecuniary legacy` 20_000 TRUE)
        EMPTY
`the Ong testacy, the daughter taking a legacy` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon, with a daughter` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon`
        (JUST `the will giving the daughter a legacy`) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(2)(c) — a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant on intestacy` `the Ong testacy, the daughter taking a legacy` "ping"
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(2)(c) — a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant on intestacy` `the Ong testacy, the daughter taking a legacy` "chan"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy, the daughter taking a legacy` "ping" FALSE EQUALS
            JUST `such person or persons, being beneficiaries under the will, as would have been entitled to a grant of letters of administration if the deceased had died intestate`
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy, the daughter taking a legacy` "chan" FALSE EQUALS
            JUST `a universal or residuary legatee`

-- THE LADDER'S ORDER, RUNG BY ADJACENT RUNG. "shall belong to the following
-- persons in the following order" is the only ranking in the grant machinery,
-- and a fixture that puts a person in one rung tests nothing about the order
-- unless he answers a LOWER rung too. Each pair below is one person who
-- answers two adjacent rungs, so each assertion fails if the two are swapped.
--   (a) over (b): Chan is the residuary legatee AND a legal personal
--       representative of a deceased residuary legatee.
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` "chan" TRUE EQUALS
            JUST `a universal or residuary legatee`
--   (b) over (c): the daughter is a beneficiary who would take on an intestacy
--       AND a legal personal representative of a deceased residuary legatee.
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy, the daughter taking a legacy` "ping" TRUE EQUALS
            JUST `a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee`
--   (c) over (d): the daughter's pecuniary legacy is a beneficial interest, so
--       rung (d) answers of her too — asserted above, where she comes out in (c).
--   (d) over (e): Lim is the creditor of this estate AND takes a beneficial
--       pecuniary legacy under this will.
`the will with a residue and a legacy to the creditor` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE
            , `a PAA gift to` `Lim Mei Ling` `a pecuniary legacy` 20_000 TRUE)
        EMPTY
`the Ong testacy, the creditor also taking a legacy` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon, with a creditor`
        (JUST `the will with a residue and a legacy to the creditor`) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(2)(e) — a creditor of the deceased` `the Ong testacy, the creditor also taking a legacy` "lim"
#ASSERT `s 13(2)(d) — a legatee having a beneficial interest` `the Ong testacy, the creditor also taking a legacy` "lim"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy, the creditor also taking a legacy` "lim" FALSE EQUALS
            JUST `a legatee having a beneficial interest`

-- s 14 — Chan is abroad and Goh is unwilling to act, so the attorney route
-- opens; make Goh willing and it closes; make Chan the sole executor and there
-- is no other executor at all, so it opens again; keep him in Singapore and it
-- closes on the first limb.
`the will whose executor is abroad, the other unwilling` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh, unwilling` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
`the will whose executor is abroad, the other willing` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
`the will whose sole executor is abroad` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon` (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor`
            `the will whose executor is abroad, the other unwilling`
            (`a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor`
                `the will whose executor is abroad, the other willing`
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor`
            `the will whose sole executor is abroad`
            (`a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- OVER-DETERMINED, AND KEPT AS SUCH: that will appoints Goh Siew Lan too, who
-- is in Singapore and willing, so the SECOND limb fails as well as the first.
#ASSERT NOT `s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor`
                `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- ... so the FIRST limb gets a minimal pair of its own. A sole executor within
-- Singapore differs from `the will whose sole executor is abroad`, which
-- satisfies the section, in exactly the fact s 14 opens with; there being no
-- other executor at all, the second limb is satisfied on both sides. Without
-- this the first limb could be deleted with the suite staying green.
`the will whose sole executor is within Singapore` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon` (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor`
                `the will whose sole executor is within Singapore`
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- ... and the SECOND limb's "within Singapore" gets one too. Goh willing but
-- ABROAD is not another executor "within Singapore willing to act", so the
-- route stays open for Chan; Goh willing and in Singapore shuts it. The pair
-- differs in Goh's absence and in nothing else, and without it the words
-- "within Singapore" could be deleted from that helper unnoticed.
`the will whose executors are both abroad` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
            , `a PAA executor` `Goh, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT     `s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor`
                `the will whose executors are both abroad`
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `another executor within Singapore willing to act`
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
                (`a PAA executor` `Goh, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `another executor within Singapore willing to act`
                (`a PAA executor` `Chan, abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
                (`a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 14 — the limitation on a grant to the attorney of an absent executor` EQUALS
            `limited in some other way` "limited until he obtains probate for himself, and in the meantime to any purpose to which the attorney’s authority is limited"

-- s 15 — THE PERSON-SIDE LIMB, which is the one an earlier draft did not test.
-- All three conjuncts get a failing case: the s 13(1) gate, membership of the
-- s 13(2) class, and absence from Singapore. The stranger assertion is the one
-- that would have caught the defect — before the repair, an absent stranger
-- with no interest in the estate satisfied the section.
`the will with a residue, the executor having extracted probate` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Goh, abroad` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE)
        EMPTY
`the Ong testacy whose executor has proved` MEANS
    `the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will with a residue, the executor having extracted probate`) EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 15 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to the attorney of an absent person entitled`
            `the Ong testacy with a creditor` `the will with a residue and a legacy` `Chan, abroad` FALSE `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 15 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to the attorney of an absent person entitled`
                `the Ong testacy with a creditor` `the will with a residue and a legacy` `a stranger abroad` FALSE `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 15 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to the attorney of an absent person entitled`
                `the Ong testacy with a creditor` `the will with a residue and a legacy` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 15 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to the attorney of an absent person entitled`
                `the Ong testacy whose executor has proved` `the will with a residue, the executor having extracted probate` `Goh, abroad` FALSE `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and the same absent stranger DOES satisfy it once limb (b) is proved of
-- him, which is the only route by which a person outside the will can stand in
-- the s 13(2) class at all.
#ASSERT `s 15 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to the attorney of an absent person entitled`
            `the Ong testacy with a creditor` `the will with a residue and a legacy` `a stranger abroad` TRUE `the date of the hearing`

-- s 22 — the bar, and the counterfactual entitlement that opens the s 22(2)
-- route. The bar is a fact already construed under the Mental Capacity Act
-- 2008 and arrives proved.
#ASSERT     `s 22(1) — no probate or letters of administration are to be granted to a person who lacks mental capacity` `Chan, lacking capacity`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) — no probate or letters of administration are to be granted to a person who lacks mental capacity` `Chan Kok Wai`
#ASSERT `s 22(2) — this person would, if he or she did not lack mental capacity, be entitled to probate or letters of administration`
            (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose sole executor lacks mental capacity`) EMPTY) `Chan, lacking capacity`
-- ... a capable executor is not within s 22(2) at all, and a person who lacks
-- capacity but is entitled to nothing is not either.
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2) — this person would, if he or she did not lack mental capacity, be entitled to probate or letters of administration`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have not extracted probate`) EMPTY) `Chan Kok Wai`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2) — this person would, if he or she did not lack mental capacity, be entitled to probate or letters of administration`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose sole executor lacks mental capacity`) EMPTY) `a stranger lacking capacity`
-- ... and the SECOND disjunct of the entitlement — the s 18(4)(a) class — which
-- had no case of its own: every fixture above reaches s 22(2) through s 8(1),
-- so the intestacy route could be deleted with the suite staying green. A widow
-- who lacks capacity is entitled to letters of administration on an intestacy
-- and to nothing under s 8(1), there being no will at all.
`Lim Mei Ling, lacking capacity` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Lim Mei Ling" "lim" `living` (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Tan Ah Kow’s family, the widow lacking capacity` MEANS
    `a PAA family` (LIST `a PAA marriage to` `Lim Mei Ling, lacking capacity` TRUE) EMPTY
`the Tan intestacy, the widow lacking capacity` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family, the widow lacking capacity` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow lacking capacity` "lim"
#ASSERT     `s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin` `the Tan intestacy, the widow lacking capacity` "lim"
#ASSERT     `s 22(2) — this person would, if he or she did not lack mental capacity, be entitled to probate or letters of administration`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow lacking capacity` `Lim Mei Ling, lacking capacity`
#ASSERT `s 22(2) — the limitation on a grant made for the use and benefit of a person who lacks mental capacity` EQUALS
            `limited in some other way` "until that person ceases to lack mental capacity and obtains a grant to himself or herself"

-- s 12 and s 16 — the three outcomes, and s 16 reaching the same answers for a
-- grant of letters of administration with the will annexed. s 12(2) is tested
-- first and displaces s 12(1), which the third and fourth pairs show.
#ASSERT `s 12 — codicil propounded after probate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing follows under section 12`
#ASSERT `s 12 — codicil propounded after probate` FALSE TRUE  EQUALS `nothing follows under section 12`
#ASSERT `s 12 — codicil propounded after probate` TRUE FALSE  EQUALS `separate probate may be granted of the codicil`
#ASSERT `s 12 — codicil propounded after probate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS
            `the probate shall be revoked, and a new probate shall be granted of the will and codicil together`
#ASSERT `s 16 — codicil propounded after grant of letters of administration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS
            `the probate shall be revoked, and a new probate shall be granted of the will and codicil together`
#ASSERT `s 16 — codicil propounded after grant of letters of administration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS
            `separate probate may be granted of the codicil`

-- s 9 — the two limbs and the two ways of failing. Limb (b) is GATED on limb
-- (a) failing in the statute's own words ("if no such copy or draft is
-- produced"), so a copy produced but not identical falls to no probate and NOT
-- to limb (b): that is the fourth assertion, and it is the one that
-- distinguishes an ordered BRANCH from a bare disjunction.
#ASSERT `s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS
            `no probate may be granted under section 9`
#ASSERT `s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS
            `probate of that copy or draft, limited until the original is admitted to probate`
#ASSERT `s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS
            `probate of the contents of the will, limited until the original is admitted to probate`
#ASSERT `s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS
            `no probate may be granted under section 9`
-- ... the opening words have TWO alternative gates, and the second one — "or
-- where a will cannot for any sufficient reason be produced" — opens the
-- section just as the first does.
#ASSERT `s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS
            `probate of that copy or draft, limited until the original is admitted to probate`
-- ... and limb (b) needs its own second conjunct: no copy, and contents that
-- CANNOT be sufficiently established, gives no probate.
#ASSERT `s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS
            `no probate may be granted under section 9`

-- s 10 — destruction by the testator takes the case outside the section, that
-- being a revocation; and the contents must be capable of being established.
#ASSERT     `s 10 — probate may be granted of a copy or draft thereof, or of the contents thereof` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — probate may be granted of a copy or draft thereof, or of the contents thereof` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — probate may be granted of a copy or draft thereof, or of the contents thereof` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — probate may be granted of a copy or draft thereof, or of the contents thereof` FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- s 11 — a CHOICE of two grants on one set of facts, so both are available
-- together and the result is a list. Without the authenticated copy there is no
-- choice at all.
#ASSERT `s 11 — administration with copy annexed of authenticated copy of will proved abroad` TRUE TRUE EQUALS
            LIST `probate`, `letters of administration with the will annexed`
#ASSERT `s 11 — administration with copy annexed of authenticated copy of will proved abroad` TRUE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 11 — administration with copy annexed of authenticated copy of will proved abroad` FALSE TRUE EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `Scenario B — a life interest, and section 6(4)'s narrower minority`

-- NO FIXTURE ABOVE CREATES A LIFE INTEREST, and AMBIGUITY A5's whole reasoning
-- rests on the limb one does. These two wills supply it: one whose life tenant
-- is alive, one whose life tenant has died. s 6(2) asks only whether a life
-- interest ARISES, so both answer TRUE; s 6(4) asks whether one SUBSISTS, and
-- only the first does.
`the will with a life interest to Goh` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE)
        (LIST `a PAA life interest to` `Goh Siew Lan`)
`the will with a life interest that has fallen in` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE)
        (LIST `a PAA life interest to` `Goh, dying after the testator`)
`letters with the will annexed to Chan alone` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`the Ong testacy with a life interest` MEANS
    `the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will with a life interest to Goh`) EMPTY
`the Ong testacy with a life interest, Chan administering` MEANS
    `the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will with a life interest to Goh`) (LIST `letters with the will annexed to Chan alone`)
`the Ong testacy, the life tenant having died` MEANS
    `the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will with a life interest that has fallen in`) EMPTY

#ASSERT `s 6(2) — a life interest arises under the will` `the Ong testacy with a life interest`
#ASSERT `s 6(2) — a life interest arises under the will` `the Ong testacy, the life tenant having died`
#ASSERT     `s 6(4) — a life interest subsists` `the Ong testacy with a life interest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — a life interest subsists` `the Ong testacy, the life tenant having died`
-- ... so the s 6(2) requirement is engaged on this estate although there is no
-- minority anywhere in it. This is the limb AMBIGUITY A5 turns on.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — there is a minority` `the Ong testacy with a life interest` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — the requirement as to the grantees is engaged` `the Ong testacy with a life interest` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and AMBIGUITY A5 taken at its word: a grant of letters of administration
-- WITH THE WILL ANNEXED is one s 6(2) governs, so a sole individual
-- administrator does not comply with it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(2) — the grant complies with section 6(2)` `the Ong testacy with a life interest` `letters with the will annexed to Chan alone` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and the s 6(4) window is open on the life-interest limb alone.
#ASSERT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Ong testacy with a life interest, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`

-- s 6(4)'s MINORITY IS OF A BENEFICIARY, and this is the pair that separates it
-- from s 6(2)'s. The will appoints an INFANT executor who takes nothing under
-- it. s 6(2) finds a minority, on AMBIGUITY A4's wide reading of its
-- unqualified words; s 6(4) does not, because an infant executor is not a
-- beneficiary. An earlier draft called s 6(2)'s predicate at the s 6(4) site,
-- so this estate opened the s 6(4) window with no beneficiary's minority in it.
`Ng Wei Jie, an infant executor` MEANS `a PAA minor` "Ng Wei Jie" "ngwj"
`the will appointing an infant executor` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Ng Wei Jie, an infant executor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE)
        EMPTY
`the Ong testacy, an infant executor, Chan administering` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon`
        (JUST `the will appointing an infant executor`)
        (LIST `letters with the will annexed to Chan alone`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Ng Wei Jie, an infant executor`) FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 6(2) — there is a minority` `the Ong testacy, an infant executor, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary` `the Ong testacy, an infant executor, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary` `the Ong testacy, an infant executor, Chan administering` `Ng Wei Jie, an infant executor`
#ASSERT     `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary` `the Ong testacy, an infant executor, Chan administering` `Chan Kok Wai`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative` `the Ong testacy, an infant executor, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and a life tenant IS a beneficiary for s 6(4), the subsection naming the
-- two in the same breath.
#ASSERT `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary` `the Ong testacy with a life interest` `Goh Siew Lan`

-- AND A BENEFICIARY IS NOT MERELY SOMEONE THE WILL GIVES SOMETHING TO. The two
-- estates below differ in ONE field of ONE disposition — `beneficial` — and in
-- nothing else: the same infant daughter, the same $20,000, the same sole
-- administrator, the same unadministered estate. Where what she takes is a
-- charge or direction for the payment of a debt she is a creditor and not a
-- beneficiary, so no minority of a beneficiary subsists and the s 6(4) window
-- is shut; where the same $20,000 is a beneficial pecuniary legacy it is open.
-- An earlier draft of `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary` read every
-- disposition, so the first estate opened the window while the same daughter,
-- on the s 13(2)(c) rule, stood in no rung of s 13(2) at all — and the third
-- assertion below is the one that pinned the contradiction down.
`Ong Li Ping, an infant` MEANS `a PAA minor` "Ong Li Ping" "ping"
`the will charging a debt in the infant daughter’s favour` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE
            , `a PAA gift to` `Ong Li Ping, an infant` `a charge or direction for the payment of a debt` 20_000 FALSE)
        EMPTY
`the will giving the infant daughter a beneficial legacy` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE
            , `a PAA gift to` `Ong Li Ping, an infant` `a pecuniary legacy` 20_000 TRUE)
        EMPTY
`the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking only a charge, Chan administering` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon`
        (JUST `the will charging a debt in the infant daughter’s favour`)
        (LIST `letters with the will annexed to Chan alone`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Ong Li Ping, an infant`) FALSE
`the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking a beneficial legacy, Chan administering` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon`
        (JUST `the will giving the infant daughter a beneficial legacy`)
        (LIST `letters with the will annexed to Chan alone`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Ong Li Ping, an infant`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary`
                `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking only a charge, Chan administering` `Ong Li Ping, an infant`
#ASSERT     `s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary`
                `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking a beneficial legacy, Chan administering` `Ong Li Ping, an infant`
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking only a charge, Chan administering` "ping" FALSE EQUALS
            NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary`
                `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking only a charge, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary`
                `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking a beneficial legacy, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative`
                `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking only a charge, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative`
                `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking a beneficial legacy, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and s 6(2)'s unqualified "if there is a minority" still finds one on
-- BOTH, which is the whole distinction between the two subsections restated on
-- one pair of facts.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) — there is a minority`
            `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking only a charge, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT `s 6(2) — there is a minority`
            `the Ong testacy, the infant daughter taking a beneficial legacy, Chan administering` `the date of the hearing`

§§ `Scenario B — sections 25 and 27`

`a grant of probate to Chan and Goh, Goh having died` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Goh, dying after the testator`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE

`letters to two administrators, one having died` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE

`letters to a sole administrator, since deceased` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan, dying after the testator`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- s 25(1) — executors take by accrual in every case; administrators do too,
-- EXCEPT where s 6 applies, which on reading A9 is the minority or
-- life-interest case. The Ong estate has neither; the Tan estate has a
-- minority. All four members of the enum are asserted.
#ASSERT `s 25(1) — death of one of several executors or administrators` (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have all extracted probate`) EMPTY) `a grant of probate to Chan and Goh, Goh having died` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `the representation of the estate accrues to the surviving executor or executors`
#ASSERT `s 25(1) — death of one of several executors or administrators` (`the Ong estate with` NOTHING EMPTY) `letters to two administrators, one having died` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `the representation of the estate accrues to the surviving administrator or administrators`
#ASSERT `s 25(1) — death of one of several executors or administrators` `the Tan intestacy` `letters to two administrators, one having died` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `the representation does not accrue, this being a case to which section 6 applies`
-- ... and where nobody has died, the subsection does not apply at all.
#ASSERT `s 25(1) — death of one of several executors or administrators` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow and the son` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `section 25(1) does not apply`
-- ... nor where the grant was to ONE person only, however dead he is:
-- "granted to more than one executor or administrator" is the subsection's own
-- threshold, and this is the other side of it.
#ASSERT `s 25(1) — death of one of several executors or administrators` (`the Ong estate with` NOTHING EMPTY) `letters to a sole administrator, since deceased` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `section 25(1) does not apply`

-- s 25(2) — a further grant on the death of an ADMINISTRATOR, of an estate not
-- fully administered. Each of the three conjuncts gets its failing case: the
-- deceased grantee must have taken as administrator (not as executor), somebody
-- must have died, and the estate must not be fully administered.
#ASSERT `s 25(2) — letters of administration may be granted in respect of any estate not fully administered`
            `the Tan intestacy` `letters to two administrators, one having died`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(2) — letters of administration may be granted in respect of any estate not fully administered`
                `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow and the son`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(2) — letters of administration may be granted in respect of any estate not fully administered`
                `the Tan intestacy, fully administered` `letters to two administrators, one having died`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(2) — letters of administration may be granted in respect of any estate not fully administered`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executors have all extracted probate`) EMPTY)
                `a grant of probate to Chan and Goh, Goh having died`

-- s 27 — a limited grant that has expired, over an estate not fully
-- administered. The mandatory case in this Act, and each of its three conjuncts
-- gets a failing case too.
`an expired limited grant` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1))
        (`limited in some other way` "limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself")
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a limited grant that has not expired` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1))
        (`limited in some other way` "limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself")
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made` `the Tan intestacy` `an expired limited grant`
-- ... this one OVER-DETERMINED, and kept for being the ordinary case: the
-- widow's grant is both unlimited and unexpired, so the first two conjuncts
-- fail together and neither is tested by it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow alone`
-- ... so "When a limited grant" gets a case of its own. This grant differs from
-- `an expired limited grant` in one field, `the limitation`, and it is a
-- deliberately impossible combination of facts — an unlimited grant cannot
-- expire by effluxion — precisely so that nothing but the first conjunct can
-- decide it. Without it that conjunct could be deleted unnoticed.
`an unlimited grant recorded as expired` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made` `the Tan intestacy` `an unlimited grant recorded as expired`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made` `the Tan intestacy` `a limited grant that has not expired`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made` `the Tan intestacy, fully administered` `an expired limited grant`


§§ `Scenario C — the Public Trustee’s small-estate powers, and the thresholds`

-- The three money thresholds in Part 11 — $50,000 (s 62), $25,000/$50,000
-- (s 63) and $10,000 (s 64) — with the s 62(2) exclusions applied and not
-- applied, and the $500 route in s 56(2). EVERY ONE OF THEM IS ASSERTED ON BOTH
-- SIDES OF ITS BOUNDARY, at the exact figure and one dollar past it, because
-- that is the only pair that distinguishes "does not exceed" from "is less
-- than".

`Wong Ah Moi` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Wong Ah Moi" "wong" (`died on` (YMD 2025 2 10)) (JUST (YMD 1980 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Wong Siew Kim`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Wong Siew Kim` MEANS `a PAA minor` "Wong Siew Kim" "kim"
`Wong Ah Moi, dying in 2000` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Wong Ah Moi" "wong" (`died on` (YMD 2000 2 10)) (JUST (YMD 1980 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Wong Siew Kim`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Wong Ah Moi, dying on 17 September 2005` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Wong Ah Moi" "wong" (`died on` (YMD 2005 9 17)) (JUST (YMD 1980 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Wong Siew Kim`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Wong Ah Moi, dying on 16 September 2005` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Wong Ah Moi" "wong" (`died on` (YMD 2005 9 16)) (JUST (YMD 1980 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Wong Siew Kim`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Wong family` MEANS `a PAA family` EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN p IS A Person, e IS AN Estate, `the applications` IS A LIST OF `Probate application`
GIVETH A `Deceased person`
`the Wong estate of` p e `the applications` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` p `the Wong family` e NOTHING EMPTY `the applications`
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Wong Siew Kim`) FALSE

-- s 62(1) — $40,000 in Singapore less $5,000 held as trustee is $35,000, so
-- the Public Trustee may declare. Raise the estate to $120,000 and he may not.
#ASSERT `s 62 — the value of the property in Singapore for the purposes of section 62` (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY) EQUALS
            35_000
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
            (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
                (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 120_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)
-- ... and the boundary: "not exceeding $50,000 in value" includes $50,000
-- exactly and excludes $50,001.
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
            (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 55_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
                (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 55_001 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)

-- s 62(2)(b) — the Dependants’ Protection Insurance exclusion is available only
-- for a death "on or after 17 September 2005", so the day itself is inside.
-- Same $20,000 of insurance moneys, two dates of death, two answers: $15,000
-- and $35,000.
#ASSERT     `s 62(2)(b) — the deceased died on or after 17 September 2005` (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 20_000 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)
#ASSERT     `s 62(2)(b) — the deceased died on or after 17 September 2005` (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi, dying on 17 September 2005` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 20_000 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 62(2)(b) — the deceased died on or after 17 September 2005` (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi, dying on 16 September 2005` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 20_000 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 62(2)(b) — the deceased died on or after 17 September 2005` (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi, dying in 2000` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 20_000 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `s 62 — the value of the property in Singapore for the purposes of section 62` (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 20_000 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY) EQUALS
            15_000
#ASSERT `s 62 — the value of the property in Singapore for the purposes of section 62` (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi, dying in 2000` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 20_000 0 0 EMPTY FALSE) EMPTY) EQUALS
            35_000

-- s 62(1) — the second gate. A PENDING application for letters of
-- administration shuts the power down; one already refused does not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
                (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
                    (LIST `a PAA application by` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `letters of administration` (JUST (YMD 2025 4 1)) `still pending`))
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
            (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
                (LIST `a PAA application by` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `letters of administration` (JUST (YMD 2025 4 1)) `refused`))
-- ... and a pending application for PROBATE is not an "application for letters
-- of administration", so it does not shut it down either.
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
            (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
                (LIST `a PAA application by` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `probate` (JUST (YMD 2025 4 1)) `still pending`))
-- ... but an application for letters WITH THE WILL ANNEXED is, on the same wide
-- reading of "letters of administration" the Act takes elsewhere. No fixture
-- exercised that disjunct, so it could have been deleted unnoticed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property`
                (`the Wong estate of` `Wong Ah Moi` (`a PAA estate` 40_000 5_000 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
                    (LIST `a PAA application by` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `letters of administration with the will annexed` (JUST (YMD 2025 4 1)) `still pending`))

-- s 62(3) — the deeming, whose only antecedent is that the declaration was made.
`the further facts, the Public Trustee having declared` MEANS
    `The further facts on which the grant machinery turns` WITH
        `the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts` IS FALSE
        `the Family Court thinks fit to require such security` IS FALSE
        `there is danger that the property may be wasted` IS FALSE
        `it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate` IS FALSE
        `the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 62(3) — the Public Trustee is empowered to administer the property as though letters of administration had been granted to him`
                `the further facts, nothing being made out`
#ASSERT `s 62(3) — the Public Trustee is empowered to administer the property as though letters of administration had been granted to him`
