-- ... and the class itself. A GRANDPARENT is next of kin for s 18(4)(a) and is
-- NOT one of the seven degrees s 56(2) names — "widower, widow, child, father,
-- mother, brother or sister". The same estate answers the two questions
-- differently, which is what a single shared class would have hidden.
GIVEN `the marriages` IS A LIST OF Marriage
      `the siblings` IS A LIST OF `Collateral relative`
      `the grandparents` IS A LIST OF Person
GIVETH A Family
`a family with grandparents` `the marriages` `the siblings` `the grandparents` MEANS
    Family WITH
        `the marriages of the deceased` IS `the marriages`
        `the father of the deceased` IS NOTHING
        `the mother of the deceased` IS NOTHING
        `the brothers and sisters of the deceased` IS `the siblings`
        `the grandparents of the deceased` IS `the grandparents`
        `the uncles and aunts of the deceased` IS EMPTY

