§§ `Scenario C — section 29, the security on a grant`

`the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family`
        (`a PAA estate` 120_000 0 0 0 0 (LIST `a PAA creditor` `Chan Kok Wai` 20_000 TRUE
                                         , `a PAA creditor` `Goh Siew Lan` 7_000 FALSE) FALSE)
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE

-- s 29(2) — $120,000 within the jurisdiction, less the $20,000 secured debt and
-- NOT the $7,000 unsecured one, is a bond of $100,000. The unsecured debt is
-- the assertion that matters: "without deduction of any debts due by the
-- deceased, other than debts secured by mortgage" is a double negative, and an
-- encoding that read it as a single one would answer $93,000.
#ASSERT `s 29(2) — the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` EQUALS
            100_000
#ASSERT `s 29(2) — the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn` `the Tan intestacy` EQUALS
            120_000

-- The ordinary position on a High Court grant of letters of administration:
-- bond by the grantee and 2 sureties. The duty is on the grantee, so it is
-- asked of one.
`the widow as administrator` MEANS `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING
`the Public Trustee as administrator` MEANS `a PAA grantee` `Public Trustee as grantee` `as administrator` NOTHING
`the widow as guardian of the infant` MEANS
    `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as the guardian of the person and property of the infant` (JUST "xin")
#ASSERT `s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow and the son` `the widow as administrator` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee and 2 sureties` 100_000

-- s 29(5) — the administrator being entitled to the whole after payment of the
-- debts, the sureties are ordinarily dispensed with. THE BOND REMAINS, and the
-- amount is unchanged: s 29(5) removes the sureties and not the security.
`the further facts, the administrator taking the whole` MEANS
    `The further facts on which the grant machinery turns` WITH
        `the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts` IS TRUE
        `the Family Court thinks fit to require such security` IS FALSE
        `there is danger that the property may be wasted` IS FALSE
        `it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate` IS FALSE
        `the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow and the son` `the widow as administrator` `the further facts, the administrator taking the whole` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee, sureties being dispensed with` 100_000

-- s 29(4) — the Public Trustee is not required to give security at all. THE
-- EXEMPTION IS HIS AND NOT THE GRANT'S: on a joint grant to him and the widow,
-- he is excused and she is not, which is the whole point of asking the
-- question grantee by grantee. The two assertions below are the same grant.
`a grant to the Public Trustee and the widow` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` `Public Trustee as grantee` `as administrator` NOTHING
            , `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the Public Trustee and the widow` `the Public Trustee as administrator` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `no security is required`
#ASSERT `s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the Public Trustee and the widow` `the widow as administrator` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee and 2 sureties` 100_000

-- s 29(8) — a Family Court grantee is NOT required to give security, unless the
-- grant is for the use and benefit of an infant, or the Family Court so thinks
-- fit. Three grants, three answers — and the decision is named for the
-- EXEMPTION, so it is TRUE when the grantee is excused.
`a Family Court grant to the widow` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `a Family Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a Family Court grant for the use and benefit of the infant` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as the guardian of the person and property of the infant` (JUST "xin"))
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1))
        (`limited in some other way` "limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself")
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `a Family Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the further facts, the Family Court requiring security` MEANS
    `The further facts on which the grant machinery turns` WITH
        `the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts` IS FALSE
        `the Family Court thinks fit to require such security` IS TRUE
        `there is danger that the property may be wasted` IS FALSE
        `it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate` IS FALSE
        `the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security`
            `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant to the widow` `the widow as administrator`
            `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security`
                `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant for the use and benefit of the infant` `the widow as guardian of the infant`
                `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security`
                `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant to the widow` `the widow as administrator`
                `the further facts, the Family Court requiring security` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and the subsection reaches a grantee "of letters of administration from a
-- Family Court" ONLY: the same widow on a High Court grant is outside it, so
-- the exemption is not made out and the ordinary s 29(7) duty stands.
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security`
                `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow alone` `the widow as administrator`
                `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and once the infant attains her majority the s 29(8)(a) limb stops
-- firing, so the exemption revives.
#ASSERT `s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security`
            `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant for the use and benefit of the infant` `the widow as guardian of the infant`
            `the further facts, nothing being made out` (YMD 2033 1 1)
-- ... and "letters of administration" here reaches BOTH kinds, on s 29(7)'s
-- own words as recorded at the site. Every fixture above is letters simpliciter,
-- so the second disjunct had no case and could have been deleted unnoticed —
-- which would have silently taken the narrow reading the note at the site
-- rejects.
`a Family Court grant with the will annexed to Chan` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `a Family Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security`
            `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant with the will annexed to Chan`
            (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
            `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT `s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant with the will annexed to Chan` (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as administrator` NOTHING) `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `no security is required`

#ASSERT `s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant to the widow` `the widow as administrator` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `no security is required`
#ASSERT `s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant for the use and benefit of the infant` `the widow as guardian of the infant` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing` EQUALS
            `security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee and 2 sureties` 100_000

-- s 29(7) reaches administrations only, so a grant of PROBATE requires none.
