#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(b) — an application made within the 6 months has not been proceeded with, or has been withdrawn or refused` `the Tan intestacy, an application refused a day late`

-- (c) a High Court grant of 1 June 2025 with the security still not given at
--     1 January 2026 — the one month having long expired. The boundary is
--     1 July 2025, and expiry is strict there too.
#ASSERT `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow alone` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow alone` `the further facts, nothing being made out` (YMD 2025 6 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow alone` `the further facts, nothing being made out` (YMD 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT     `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow alone` `the further facts, nothing being made out` (YMD 2025 7 2)
-- ... and where the security HAS been given, never.
`a grant to the widow, the security given` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant to the widow, the security given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and — the repair recorded above — where s 29(8) excuses the grantee from
-- giving security at all, there is nothing to neglect, however long he waits.
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant to the widow` `the further facts, nothing being made out` (YMD 2026 6 15)
-- ... and the limb reaches "letters of administration with or without the will
-- annexed" in terms, so a grant of the second kind is within it. No fixture
-- exercised that disjunct.
`letters with the will annexed to the widow, the security not given` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `letters with the will annexed to the widow, the security not given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... A GRANT OF PROBATE IS OUTSIDE THE LIMB, and this negative is
-- IRREDUCIBLY OVER-DETERMINED — deliberately so, and worth saying why rather
-- than leaving a reader to wonder. The kind-of-grant conjunct carries the
-- limb's opening words, "where any person, who has received a grant of letters
-- of administration with or without the will annexed"; but s 29(7) requires
-- security of administrations only, so `security is lawfully required of some
-- grantee` is FALSE of every grant of probate anyway. The first conjunct is
-- therefore ENTAILED by the third and cannot be given a case that fails it
-- alone. It is kept because the limb's own words name the class, and an
-- encoding that dropped them would be reading s 55(1)(c) off s 29 rather than
-- off s 55.
`a grant of probate to Chan, the security not given` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant of probate to Chan, the security not given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `security is lawfully required of some grantee` `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a grant of probate to Chan, the security not given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`

-- (d) both of s 39's and s 55(1)(d)'s own judgements made out, and each on its
--     own is not enough.
`the further facts, a receiver being insufficient` MEANS
    `The further facts on which the grant machinery turns` WITH
        `the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts` IS FALSE
        `the Family Court thinks fit to require such security` IS FALSE
        `there is danger that the property may be wasted` IS TRUE
        `it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate` IS TRUE
        `the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property` IS FALSE
`the further facts, a danger of waste only` MEANS
    `The further facts on which the grant machinery turns` WITH
        `the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts` IS FALSE
        `the Family Court thinks fit to require such security` IS FALSE
        `there is danger that the property may be wasted` IS TRUE
        `it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate` IS FALSE
        `the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property` IS FALSE
`the further facts, a receiver insufficient but no danger of waste` MEANS
    `The further facts on which the grant machinery turns` WITH
        `the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts` IS FALSE
        `the Family Court thinks fit to require such security` IS FALSE
        `there is danger that the property may be wasted` IS FALSE
        `it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate` IS TRUE
        `the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property` IS FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection` `the Tan intestacy` `the further facts, a receiver being insufficient`
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection` `the Tan intestacy` `the further facts, a danger of waste only`
-- ... and the OTHER single failing case, which was missing: s 39's danger of
-- waste absent while s 55(1)(d)'s own judgement is made out. Without it the
-- waste conjunct could be deleted with the suite staying green, both other
-- negatives failing on the protection conjunct as well.
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection` `the Tan intestacy` `the further facts, a receiver insufficient but no danger of waste`
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection` `the Tan intestacy` `the further facts, nothing being made out`
-- ... and s 39's own opening words, reproduced here to the depth this limb
-- needs: "Where any person dies leaving property within Singapore". An estate
-- with nothing in Singapore is outside s 39 and so outside this limb.
`the Tan intestacy, nothing in Singapore` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` (`a PAA estate` 0 0 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection` `the Tan intestacy, nothing in Singapore` `the further facts, a receiver being insufficient`

-- (e) letters of administration granted but never extracted. A grant of
--     PROBATE that has not been extracted is not within the limb, which speaks
--     of "an administrator".
`a grant to the widow, not extracted` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the grant not extracted` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow` NOTHING
        (LIST `a grant to the widow, not extracted`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
`a grant of probate not extracted` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 55(1)(e) — an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy, the grant not extracted`
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(e) — an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant`
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(e) — an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration` (`the Ong estate with` NOTHING (LIST `a grant of probate not extracted`))
-- ... and a grant WITH the will annexed is an administration too, which no
-- fixture exercised: the second disjunct of `a grant of letters of
-- administration that has not been extracted` could have been deleted unnoticed.
`letters with the will annexed to Chan, not extracted` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55(1)(e) — an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration` (`the Ong estate with` NOTHING (LIST `letters with the will annexed to Chan, not extracted`))

-- (f) the sole administrator having died on 1 June 2025, six months have
--     elapsed at 1 January 2026 and nobody has applied. The boundary is
--     1 December 2025.
`Lim Mei Ling, deceased` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Lim Mei Ling" "lim" (`died on` (YMD 2025 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 1 1)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a grant to the widow, since deceased` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling, deceased`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the administrator having died` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow` NOTHING
        (LIST `a grant to the widow, since deceased`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the administrator having died, an application made` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow` NOTHING
        (LIST `a grant to the widow, since deceased`)
        (LIST `a PAA application by` (`an individual` `Tan Wei`) `letters of administration` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 15)) `still pending`)
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the administrator having died` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the administrator having died` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the administrator having died` (YMD 2025 12 1)
#ASSERT     `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the administrator having died` (YMD 2025 12 2)
-- ... and an application for the representation of the estate defeats the limb.
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the administrator having died, an application made` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... an estate with a LIVING administrator is not within the limb at all ...
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and neither is an estate with NO personal representative, which has no
-- "last surviving" one. That case is limb (a)'s, and (a) is made out on it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... nor is an estate one of whose two administrators is still living: the
-- words "a last surviving executor or administrator" presuppose that none is
-- left, and the LAST is the operative one here. This
-- negative is OVER-DETERMINED and cannot be otherwise: `all have died` and
-- `six months have elapsed since the last of them died` are both `all` over the
-- same list, and a living representative has no date of death, so a fixture
-- that fails the first necessarily fails the second. Kept because the case —
-- one administrator of two having died — is exactly the one s 25(1) sends to
-- the survivor rather than to the Public Trustee.
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, one of two administrators having died` `the date of the hearing`

-- THE GATE AS A WHOLE. It is a disjunction of six limbs, and a fixture that
-- fires two of them tests neither: mutation showed that on the facts below —
-- an estate with no grant of its own, six months run, and the widow's
-- unsecured grant handed in as `g` — limbs (a) and (c) BOTH fire, so any one
-- limb could be deleted from the disjunction with every assertion staying
-- green. The six assertions that follow fire exactly one limb each.
#ASSERT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
            `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow alone` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
                `the Tan intestacy, the widow having taken a grant` `a Family Court grant to the widow`
                `the further facts, nothing being made out` (YMD 2025 5 1)

-- (a) ALONE — six months and no application, with a grant whose security HAS
--     been given, so (c) is off.
#ASSERT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
            `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow, the security given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
-- (b) ALONE — an application made inside the six months and refused, which
--     turns (a) off by making an application exist at all.
#ASSERT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
            `the Tan intestacy, an application refused` `a grant to the widow, the security given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
-- (c) ALONE — an application made and proceeded with, so (a) and (b) are both
--     off, and the widow's grant still unsecured a month on.
#ASSERT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
            `the Tan intestacy, an application proceeded with` `a grant to the widow alone` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
-- (d) ALONE — the same application, a secured grant, and s 55(1)(d)'s two
--     judgements made out.
#ASSERT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
            `the Tan intestacy, an application proceeded with` `a grant to the widow, the security given` `the further facts, a receiver being insufficient` `the date of the hearing`
-- (e) ALONE — a grant of letters of administration in the estate's own record
--     that has never been extracted, with an application proceeded with to
--     switch (a) and (b) off.
`the Tan intestacy, the grant not extracted, an application proceeded with` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow` NOTHING
        (LIST `a grant to the widow, not extracted`)
        (LIST `a PAA application by` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `letters of administration` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `proceeded with`)
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
            `the Tan intestacy, the grant not extracted, an application proceeded with` `a grant to the widow, the security given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`
-- (f) ALONE, and it takes an unusual fixture to isolate, because (f) itself
--     requires that no application has been made — which is half of (a). The
--     other half of (a) is that six months have run FROM THE DEATH, and that
--     is FALSE where the date of death is not in evidence, on the AMBIGUITY A1
--     discipline. So an intestate whose own date of death is unknown, whose
--     sole administrator died on a known date more than six months ago, and
--     for whose estate nobody has since applied, is within (f) and outside
--     every other limb.
`Tan Ah Kow, the date of death not known` MEANS
    `a PAA person in full` "Tan Ah Kow" "tan" `dead, the date of death not known` (JUST (YMD 1975 1 1))
        (LIST `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Wei`, `a PAA legitimate child` `Tan Xin`)
        FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan intestacy, the date of death not known, the administrator having died` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow, the date of death not known` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` `the estate of Tan Ah Kow`
        NOTHING (LIST `a grant to the widow, since deceased`) EMPTY
        (LIST `a PAA infant concerned in the estate` `Tan Xin`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 55(1)(a) — six months have expired from the death and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the date of death not known, the administrator having died` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made` `the Tan intestacy, the date of death not known, the administrator having died` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT `s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay`
            `the Tan intestacy, the date of death not known, the administrator having died` `a grant to the widow, the security given` `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`

§§ `Scenario D — sections 18(2), 23, 26, 30, 35(1) and 5(1)`

