#ASSERT     `s 23 — letters of administration limited to trust property may be granted` `the Ong estate holding trust property, the executor unwilling` `the date of the hearing`

-- ... AND A DEAD ONE IS NOT A REPRESENTATIVE EITHER, which the executor limb
-- did not ask. `s 13(1)(b) — this executor is disqualified` is blind to death
-- by design — death is s 13(1)'s limbs (c) and (d), not (b) — so borrowing it
-- alone made a dead executor "able and willing to act" and shut the s 23 route.
-- Each of the three estates below differs from
-- `the Ong estate holding trust property, an executor standing`, on which s 23
-- is correctly FALSE, in exactly one fact: that the representative is dead.
--
-- The FIRST is the case that cannot be defended on any reading: Chan died on
-- 1 June 2024, before the testator's death on 15 January 2025, so he never
-- became a representative at all — and this module's own
-- `s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator` exists to say so.
`the Ong estate holding trust property, the executor having predeceased` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate holding trust property`
        (JUST `the will whose executor predeceased the testator`) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
`the Ong estate holding trust property, the executor having died` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate holding trust property`
        (JUST `the will whose executor died after the testator`) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
`the Ong estate holding trust property, the administrator having died` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate holding trust property`
        NOTHING (LIST `letters to a sole administrator, since deceased`) EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23 — the deceased leaves a representative who is able and willing to act` `the Ong estate holding trust property, the executor having predeceased` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 23 — letters of administration limited to trust property may be granted` `the Ong estate holding trust property, the executor having predeceased` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23 — the deceased leaves a representative who is able and willing to act` `the Ong estate holding trust property, the executor having died` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 23 — letters of administration limited to trust property may be granted` `the Ong estate holding trust property, the executor having died` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... and the GRANTEE limb had the same blind spot, `a representative willing
-- to act` reading `willing to act` off a person without asking whether he was
-- alive to be willing.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23 — the deceased leaves a representative who is able and willing to act` `the Ong estate holding trust property, the administrator having died` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT     `s 23 — letters of administration limited to trust property may be granted` `the Ong estate holding trust property, the administrator having died` `the date of the hearing`
-- ... while a LIVING administrator still shuts it, so the repair narrows
-- nothing it should not.
`the Ong estate holding trust property, an administrator standing` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate holding trust property`
        NOTHING (LIST `letters with the will annexed to Chan alone`) EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 23 — the deceased leaves a representative who is able and willing to act` `the Ong estate holding trust property, an administrator standing` `the date of the hearing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23 — letters of administration limited to trust property may be granted` `the Ong estate holding trust property, an administrator standing` `the date of the hearing`

-- THE LIMITATIONS, which are outputs and not tests, and which the Wills Act
-- reads back out of `Limitation on the grant`.
#ASSERT `s 23 — the limitation on a grant of trust property` EQUALS `limited to settled land or to trust property`
#ASSERT `s 24 — the limitation on a grant to collect and preserve property` EQUALS
            `a grant that does not permit the distribution of the testator’s estate`

-- s 26(2) — a further grant of the excepted part, available exactly where a
-- part was excepted under s 26(1) and not otherwise.
`a grant excepting part of the estate` MEANS
    Grant WITH
        `the kind of grant` IS `letters of administration`
        `the grantees` IS LIST (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        `the date of the grant` IS JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)
        `the limitation` IS `not limited`
        `the court that made the grant` IS (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`)
        `the exception subject to which the grant is made` IS JUST "the immovable property situated outside Singapore"
        `expired by effluxion of time or by the happening of the event or contingency on which it was limited` IS FALSE
        `revoked` IS FALSE
        `has given such security as is lawfully required to be furnished` IS TRUE
        `has been extracted` IS TRUE
        `sealed under section 47(1) of the Probate and Administration Act 1934` IS FALSE
        `the date of the sealing` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT     `s 26(2) — a further grant may be made of the part of the estate excepted` `a grant excepting part of the estate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(2) — a further grant may be made of the part of the estate excepted` `a grant to the widow alone`

-- s 30 — the creditor-administrator's bond. Lim is a creditor of the Ong estate
-- and takes letters of administration there. AMBIGUITY A11 is what makes the
-- second assertion TRUE: the same creditor taking letters WITH the will annexed
-- is within s 30 too, s 13(2)(e) having expressly ranked him for that grant. A
-- grant of PROBATE is not, s 30 speaking only of letters of administration.
`letters of administration to the creditor Lim` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`letters with the will annexed to the creditor Lim` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
`probate to the creditor Lim` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `the General Division of the High Court`) TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 30 — letters of administration are granted to a creditor` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` `letters of administration to the creditor Lim`
#ASSERT     `s 30 — letters of administration are granted to a creditor` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` `letters with the will annexed to the creditor Lim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30 — letters of administration are granted to a creditor` `the Ong testacy with a creditor` `probate to the creditor Lim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30 — letters of administration are granted to a creditor` `the Tan intestacy` `letters of administration to the creditor Lim`

-- s 35(1) — a pre-2015 District Court grant over an estate later found to be
-- worth more than $3 million is saved. A High Court grant is not within the
-- subsection at all, and neither is an estate at or below the threshold: FALSE
-- there means "the saving has nothing to do", NOT "the grant is invalid".
-- "exceeds $3 million" is asserted on both sides, at the figure and a dollar up.
`a District Court grant made in 2014` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `letters of administration`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2014 6 1)) `not limited`
        `a District Court, the grant having been made before 1 January 2015` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`the Tan estate, worth more than three million` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` (`a PAA estate` 4_000_000 0 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
`the Tan estate, worth exactly three million` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` (`a PAA estate` 3_000_000 0 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
`the Tan estate, worth a dollar more than three million` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Tan Ah Kow` `Tan Ah Kow’s family` (`a PAA estate` 3_000_001 0 0 0 0 EMPTY FALSE)
        NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 35(1) — the saving in section 35(1) applies to this grant` `the Tan estate, worth more than three million` `a District Court grant made in 2014`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(1) — the saving in section 35(1) applies to this grant` `the Tan estate, worth more than three million` `a grant to the widow alone`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(1) — the saving in section 35(1) applies to this grant` `the Tan intestacy` `a District Court grant made in 2014`
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(1) — the saving in section 35(1) applies to this grant` `the Tan estate, worth exactly three million` `a District Court grant made in 2014`
#ASSERT     `s 35(1) — the saving in section 35(1) applies to this grant` `the Tan estate, worth a dollar more than three million` `a District Court grant made in 2014`

-- s 5(1) — the renouncing executor is precluded from applying thereafter, and
-- so is anyone else who renounces: s 3(1)'s class is "Any person who is or may
-- become entitled to any probate or letters of administration", which on an
-- intestacy is a widow or a next of kin and not an executor at all. The general
-- form is asserted first, and the executor form is the same rule read off the
-- one field the shared ontology has for it.
#ASSERT     `s 5(1) — the person so renouncing is precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 5(1) — the person so renouncing is precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration` FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 5(1) — precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration` (`a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 5(1) — precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration` (`a PAA executor` `Goh Siew Lan` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- THE FOUR INERT CARRIERS STAY `#EVAL`, AND THE REASON IS NOT LAZINESS. An
-- inert carrier is a chain of statutory strings joined by the AND-sugar, and
-- such a chain evaluates to TRUE unconditionally — the strings contribute
-- nothing to the truth value. So `#ASSERT` on one of them would pass whatever
-- the strings said, including nothing at all: it would raise the assertion
-- count by four and test zero propositions, which is worse than not asserting,
-- because a green count is read as coverage. What these carriers are FOR is
-- that a reader running the file sees the text of a provision the module read
-- and declined, and can tell it apart from a provision that is not in the Act.
-- ss 34 and 36 are repealed and have no operative words at all; s 6(3) is
-- evidential and is load-bearing for AMBIGUITY A2; s 55(2) is a saving that
-- confers nothing; s 2 is the definitional residue.
#EVAL `ss 34 and 36 — repealed, and therefore not encoded`
#EVAL `s 2 — the definitions the grant machinery reads`
#EVAL `s 6(3) — prima facie evidence of a minority or life interest (not encoded)`
#EVAL `s 55(2) — the six-month periods do not prevent the Public Trustee from applying sooner`

§§ `The deontic outcomes, exercised`

-- A `DEONTIC` VALUE CANNOT BE `EQUALS`-COMPARED, so the four regulative rules
-- below stay `#EVAL` and `#TRACE`, and what is ASSERTED is the boolean guard
-- that decides which arm each of them takes. That is the whole of the
-- statable content: whether the duty arises, and on whom.

-- s 28 — the duty and its s 28(2) exemption. The exempt class is asserted in
-- s 28(2)'s own words, and it does not travel from s 6(6): the two decisions
-- happen to agree on this ontology's members, which is why both are asserted
-- rather than one being taken as the other.
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(2) — the grantee is the Public Trustee or a trust company` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`)
#ASSERT     `s 28(2) — the grantee is the Public Trustee or a trust company` `Public Trustee as grantee`
#ASSERT     `s 28(2) — the grantee is the Public Trustee or a trust company` `Acme Trust Company`
#ASSERT NOT `s 28(2) — the grantee is the Public Trustee or a trust company` `the Government`
-- An individual grantee owes the oath; the Public Trustee does not, so his rule
-- collapses to FULFILLED before any event stream is applied.
#EVAL `s 28 — the grantee shall take an oath` (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Lim Mei Ling`) `as administrator` NOTHING)
#EVAL `s 28 — the grantee shall take an oath` (`a PAA grantee` `Public Trustee as grantee` `as administrator` NOTHING)

-- s 29(7) with s 55(1)(c) — the only duty in this Act with both a deadline and
-- a named consequence. Performed inside the month, it is FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 29(7) — the grantee shall give security for the due administration of the estate` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the grantee` DOES `give security for the due administration of the estate` AT 10

-- Not performed. The LEST arm opens the s 55(1)(c) consequence, and this trace
-- shows the court EXERCISING it: letters of administration to the Public
-- Trustee. Because s 55(1) says such letters "may be granted", the arm is a MAY
-- and not a penalty — so the court's declining to exercise it would be no
-- breach either, and the residual would collapse to FULFILLED rather than to a
-- violation. The trace below is the exercise; the non-exercise is the reason
-- the arm is written MAY, and is asserted nowhere because a MAY has nothing to
-- assert about an omission.
#TRACE `s 29(7) — the grantee shall give security for the due administration of the estate` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `grant letters of administration with or without the will annexed to the Public Trustee` AT 40

-- Where no security is required at all there is nothing owed.
#EVAL `s 29(7) — the grantee shall give security for the due administration of the estate` FALSE

-- s 12(2) — mandatory. The court owes the revocation and re-grant exactly when
-- s 12 answers with the revocation member, which is the assertion above.
#EVAL `s 12(2) — the probate shall be revoked and a new probate granted` (`s 12 — codicil propounded after probate` TRUE TRUE)
#EVAL `s 12(2) — the probate shall be revoked and a new probate granted` (`s 12 — codicil propounded after probate` TRUE FALSE)
#TRACE `s 12(2) — the probate shall be revoked and a new probate granted` (`s 12 — codicil propounded after probate` TRUE TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `revoke the probate and grant a new probate of the will and codicil together` AT 5

-- s 27 — the other mandatory grant. Its guard is asserted above, on both sides.
#EVAL `s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted` `the Tan intestacy` `an expired limited grant`
#EVAL `s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted` `the Tan intestacy` `a grant to the widow alone`


§§ `Three limbs the inert prose quotes — asserted before they were tested`

-- EACH OF THE THREE ASSERTIONS BELOW FAILED WHEN IT WAS FIRST WRITTEN, and each
-- named a limb that the string beside the node quoted and the node did not
-- test. They are kept here, in one place, because they are the same defect
-- three times over and a reader who has met it once should be able to find the
-- other two.

-- (1) s 8(3) — "where more than one person is appointed an executor by a will".
-- A will appointing a single executor is s 8(1)'s case and not s 8(3)'s, so the
-- subsection has no application to it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(3) — probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed, subject to section 6`
                (`the Ong estate with` (JUST `the will whose executor is willing`) EMPTY) `a grant of probate to Chan alone`

-- (2) s 29(8) — "A grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court".
-- The subsection exempts a grantee of letters of administration and says
-- nothing of a grantee of probate, so no s 29(8) exemption is made out on a
-- Family Court grant of probate.
`a Family Court grant of probate to Chan` MEANS
    `a PAA grant` `probate`
        (LIST `a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING)
        (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `not limited`
        (`a court within the meaning of these Acts` `a Family Court`) FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security`
                `the Tan estate, with a mortgage debt` `a Family Court grant of probate to Chan`
                (`a PAA grantee` (`an individual` `Chan Kok Wai`) `as executor` NOTHING)
                `the further facts, nothing being made out` `the date of the hearing`

-- (3) s 13(2)(c) — "such person or persons, being beneficiaries under the
-- will". A charge or direction for the payment of a debt is not a beneficial
-- gift: Wills Act 1838 s 10(1) says so in terms, sparing an attesting witness's
-- gift where what he takes is "other than and except charges and directions for
-- the payment of any debt". That is
-- why `Disposition` carries `beneficial` as a separate field. A daughter whose
-- only interest under the will is such a charge is not a beneficiary under it,
-- so she stands in no rung of s 13(2) at all — not in (c), and not in (d)
-- either, which needs the same beneficial interest.
`the will charging a debt in the daughter’s favour` MEANS
    `a PAA will of` `Ong Bee Hoon, with a daughter`
        (LIST `a PAA executor` `Chan Kok Wai` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
        (LIST `a PAA gift to` `Chan Kok Wai` `a residuary gift` 300_000 TRUE
            , `a PAA gift to` `Ong Li Ping` `a charge or direction for the payment of a debt` 20_000 FALSE)
        EMPTY
`the Ong testacy, the will charging a debt in the daughter’s favour` MEANS
    `a PAA deceased person` `Ong Bee Hoon, with a daughter` `Ong Bee Hoon’s family` `the estate of Ong Bee Hoon`
        (JUST `the will charging a debt in the daughter’s favour`) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 13(2)(c) — a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant on intestacy` `the Ong testacy, the will charging a debt in the daughter’s favour` "ping"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands` `the Ong testacy, the will charging a debt in the daughter’s favour` "ping" FALSE EQUALS
            NOTHING
